3031217e4df5b267e3bbb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/c941e375468725825023031217e4df5b267e3bbb","node_id":"C_kwDOSa1B6doAKGM5NDFlMzc1NDY4NzI1ODI1MDIzMDMxMjE3ZTRkZjViMjY3ZTNiYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/bccd65b21275014499388374ec2f33236f339fd0","sha":"bccd65b21275014499388374ec2f33236f339fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/bccd65b21275014499388374ec2f33236f339fd0"}],"sha":"c941e375468725825023031217e4df5b267e3bbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/c941e375468725825023031217e4df5b267e3bbb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/bccd65b21275014499388374ec2f33236f339fd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T06:26:07Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T06:26:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"assistant-fs-tools: filesystem read/write tools for the Assistant (#40)\n\n* stage 1: resolve open questions in SCOPE.md\n\nRecord decisions for the assistant-fs-tools job in\n`.codeless/jobs/assistant-fs-tools/SCOPE.md` under \"Decisions\":\n\n- D1 confirms the three-mode vocabulary (`read-only` /\n  `approve-edits` / `bypass`) as the wire values, with a\n  server-side enum gate.\n- D2 confirms `mode TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''read-only''` as a column\n  on `assistant_threads` (no separate table, no CHECK constraint).\n- D3 confirms `.codeless/jobs/<name>/` writes always route through\n  `jobs.updateScope`, including in `bypass`, so the paused-job rule\n  remains a runtime invariant rather than a permission.\n- D4–D8 resolve the five numbered open questions per their stated\n  biases: canonicalising sandbox, 5 MiB read cap, 200-match search\n  cap with truncation flag, reuse of the existing diff action-card\n  for `fs.write` confirmations, and hiding write tools from the\n  planner''s tool list on `read-only` threads (with server-side\n  rejection retained as defence-in-depth).\n\nProse-only stage; no code changed. Stage 3 onward treats the\n\"Decisions\" section as authoritative.\n\n* stage 0: resolve open questions in SCOPE.md — confirm the three mode names (bias read-only / approve-edits / bypass to match Claude Code), confirm thread-mode storage (column on assistant_threads), confirm the .codeless/jobs/<name>/ special case routes through jobs.updateScope even in bypass; record decisions in SCOPE.md\n\n* stage 3: add `mode` column to assistant_threads (migration, default ''read-only''); add assistant.setThreadMode(thread_id, mode) RPC; round-trip tests\n\n* stage 2: add `mode` column to assistant_threads (migration, default ''read-only''); add assistant.setThreadMode(thread_id, mode) RPC; round-trip tests\n\n* stage 4: read-only fs tools for assistant threads\n\nAdds fs.list, fs.read, fs.search Tool impls under\ncodeless-tools::fs, a workspace-root path Sandbox that rejects\nabsolute paths and `..` traversal (canonicalising both root and\ntarget so a symlink whose target escapes the root is rejected the\nsame way as a literal traversal), and\nregister_assistant_thread_read_tools so the planner can wire the\nthree onto a per-thread ToolRegistry in stage 5.\n\nPer-tool unit tests cover happy path, sandbox rejects (absolute,\nparent traversal, symlink escape), and per-tool caps (5 MiB read,\n200-match search, binary-file skip). tests/fs_tools.rs is the\nregistry-level integration test: dispatches list -> read -> search\nthrough ToolRegistry::get the way codeless-mcp will, and pins that\nthe same sandbox is wired into all three tools so a regression\nthat unwires one slips none.\n\nignore = \"0.4\" is the new dependency (gitignore-aware traversal +\nglobset re-export for fs.search''s `glob` arg); regex = \"1\" was\nalready in the workspace''s transitive tree but is now a direct\ndep so codeless-tools owns the version pin.\n\n* stage 3: implement read-only fs tools (fs.list, fs.read, fs.search) in codeless-tools with a workspace-root path sandbox that rejects absolute paths and `..` traversal; register on the planner''s tool registry for assistant threads only; per-tool unit tests plus an integration test using MockRunner\n\n* stage 4: read-only end-to-end before write paths land\n\n* stage 6: implement write fs tools (fs.write, fs.edit) gated by thread mode; `approve-edits` surfaces each write as an AssistantActionCard the user confirms via the existing confirm_assistant_action dispatcher; `bypass` writes through; writes under `.codeless/jobs/<name>/` route through `jobs.updateScope` in every mode; tests for each mode and for the job-scope special case\n\n* stage 5: implement write fs tools (fs.write, fs.edit) gated by thread mode; `approve-edits` surfaces each write as an AssistantActionCard the user confirms via the existing confirm_assistant_action dispatcher; `bypass` writes through; writes under `.codeless/jobs/<name>/` route through `jobs.updateScope` in every mode; tests for each mode and for the job-scope special case\n\n* stage 7: UI — mode dropdown in the /assistant context panel (right rail per ASSISTANT-SCOPE §1) calling assistant.setThreadMode; display reflects server state (R4); pnpm typecheck green\n\n* stage 6: UI — mode dropdown in the /assistant context panel (right rail per ASSISTANT-SCOPE §1) calling assistant.setThreadMode; display reflects server state (R4); pnpm typecheck green","tree":{"sha":"38a10cba32a0bb58a3897ccab0c0f28d1cafb83f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/38a10cba32a0bb58a3897ccab0c0f28d1cafb83f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/bccd65b21275014499388374ec2f33236f339fd0","verification":{"payload":"tree 38a10cba32a0bb58a3897ccab0c0f28d1cafb83f\nparent e238f5915ed3923117e125b212d40d3e9a275775\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1779171967 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779171967 +0800\n\nassistant-fs-tools: filesystem read/write tools for the Assistant (#40)\n\n* stage 1: resolve open questions in SCOPE.md\n\nRecord decisions for the assistant-fs-tools job in\n`.codeless/jobs/assistant-fs-tools/SCOPE.md` under \"Decisions\":\n\n- D1 confirms the three-mode vocabulary (`read-only` /\n  `approve-edits` / `bypass`) as the wire values, with a\n  server-side enum gate.\n- D2 confirms `mode TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''read-only''` as a column\n  on `assistant_threads` (no separate table, no CHECK constraint).\n- D3 confirms `.codeless/jobs/<name>/` writes always route through\n  `jobs.updateScope`, including in `bypass`, so the paused-job rule\n  remains a runtime invariant rather than a permission.\n- D4–D8 resolve the five numbered open questions per their stated\n  biases: canonicalising sandbox, 5 MiB read cap, 200-match search\n  cap with truncation flag, reuse of the existing diff action-card\n  for `fs.write` confirmations, and hiding write tools from the\n  planner''s tool list on `read-only` threads (with server-side\n  rejection retained as defence-in-depth).\n\nProse-only stage; no code changed. Stage 3 onward treats the\n\"Decisions\" section as authoritative.\n\n* stage 0: resolve open questions in SCOPE.md — confirm the three mode names (bias read-only / approve-edits / bypass to match Claude Code), confirm thread-mode storage (column on assistant_threads), confirm the .codeless/jobs/<name>/ special case routes through jobs.updateScope even in bypass; record decisions in SCOPE.md\n\n* stage 3: add `mode` column to assistant_threads (migration, default ''read-only''); add assistant.setThreadMode(thread_id, mode) RPC; round-trip tests\n\n* stage 2: add `mode` column to assistant_threads (migration, default ''read-only''); add assistant.setThreadMode(thread_id, mode) RPC; round-trip tests\n\n* stage 4: read-only fs tools for assistant threads\n\nAdds fs.list, fs.read, fs.search Tool impls under\ncodeless-tools::fs, a workspace-root path Sandbox that rejects\nabsolute paths and `..` traversal (canonicalising both root and\ntarget so a symlink whose target escapes the root is rejected the\nsame way as a literal traversal), and\nregister_assistant_thread_read_tools so the planner can wire the\nthree onto a per-thread ToolRegistry in stage 5.\n\nPer-tool unit tests cover happy path, sandbox rejects (absolute,\nparent traversal, symlink escape), and per-tool caps (5 MiB read,\n200-match search, binary-file skip). tests/fs_tools.rs is the\nregistry-level integration test: dispatches list -> read -> search\nthrough ToolRegistry::get the way codeless-mcp will, and pins that\nthe same sandbox is wired into all three tools so a regression\nthat unwires one slips none.\n\nignore = \"0.4\" is the new dependency (gitignore-aware traversal +\nglobset re-export for fs.search''s `glob` arg); regex = \"1\" was\nalready in the workspace''s transitive tree but is now a direct\ndep so codeless-tools owns the version pin.\n\n* stage 3: implement read-only fs tools (fs.list, fs.read, fs.search) in codeless-tools with a workspace-root path sandbox that rejects absolute paths and `..` traversal; register on the planner''s tool registry for assistant threads only; per-tool unit tests plus an integration test using MockRunner\n\n* stage 4: read-only end-to-end before write paths land\n\n* stage 6: implement write fs tools (fs.write, fs.edit) gated by thread mode; `approve-edits` surfaces each write as an AssistantActionCard the user confirms via the existing confirm_assistant_action dispatcher; `bypass` writes through; writes under `.codeless/jobs/<name>/` route through `jobs.updateScope` in every mode; tests for each mode and for the job-scope special case\n\n* stage 5: implement write fs tools (fs.write, fs.edit) gated by thread mode; `approve-edits` surfaces each write as an AssistantActionCard the user confirms via the existing confirm_assistant_action dispatcher; `bypass` writes through; writes under `.codeless/jobs/<name>/` route through `jobs.updateScope` in every mode; tests for each mode and for the job-scope special case\n\n* stage 7: UI — mode dropdown in the /assistant context panel (right rail per ASSISTANT-SCOPE §1) calling assistant.setThreadMode; display reflects server state (R4); pnpm typecheck green\n\n* stage 6: UI — mode dropdown in the /assistant context panel (right rail per ASSISTANT-SCOPE §1) calling assistant.setThreadMode; display reflects server state (R4); pnpm typecheck green","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDAJ/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0c4QAEYcMaAqu4No1MZdVKUT1fbh\n7OSu0MYGkMReviQmP5syGLuuYXB8JBOBtcuZkE3wte4hGqO6Cr5txIx7dQY+rNeW\ni12XxmhY76JXddVQjiUzGDLmJ18CWiC/L12IVRQ6w1cb3IsdAKYJ+OY9W5ujjfHr\n5+RDKW0bYj5bqHueiqBlHkOpyown3lG5bxCBUPjNx8N/FUlU5ZLav+gLqH2rB1hM\nhv9MG6WLGOqL/LB5xVWv9r/hrJh26Lv0H5M0kP3au22/R0Ah6ADy8rSytyr3YUDs\nEh16mKyXtT7KUXIzQu0NF6sOvbhbm/Ttc0AOc/PCF7C13fiiRmVisC31OGy2JNzK\nRU1CI3RsH0H8EWKVWJ9VzWBUCCBS8mYvTV3sXXXKqO6tllAngnU8Zevf0OSB+x75\ncKUjHLwoGdY8fEOuulNnGn+VBAMwvxH3eC3/OosR/S3KZQbd7dOBcSZTeqgG9hbm\nwIxY8Fa0kftKLgEcqwLHO9dr5iDaKInVQU1wxdR/AYBZ6SfY2eb4Mcqx2IWLu8ug\nN0ZiOV6nRglXQHBjZg7NUFCUQ9dGaHINN5IoRkrOxQ5xXMA4RIa/yoY9LZeaTfhd\n3J4YfwJNZ+oSVgorKKXIJ8dK2L1uL7xdkSHAULk5e3jiNnGNRM8hTxGyQq/rypaf\nDDU1n3jskEJ670nPgyY0\n=ZiwN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T06:26:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/r