ess/commits/0bafa6b6833a4f5b364e6804c44a9a9ae7f7b7a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T05:09:43Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T05:09:43Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"scaffold job: assistant-fs-tools","tree":{"sha":"73e03dbff2b555f59f6e2f7145fcbe6f795cb025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/73e03dbff2b555f59f6e2f7145fcbe6f795cb025"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/0bafa6b6833a4f5b364e6804c44a9a9ae7f7b7a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/0bafa6b6833a4f5b364e6804c44a9a9ae7f7b7a5","node_id":"C_kwDOSa1B6doAKDBiYWZhNmI2ODMzYTRmNWIzNjRlNjgwNGM0NGE5YTlhZTdmN2I3YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86","sha":"2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86"}],"sha":"0bafa6b6833a4f5b364e6804c44a9a9ae7f7b7a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/0bafa6b6833a4f5b364e6804c44a9a9ae7f7b7a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T04:22:13Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T04:22:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Codeless/workspace scoping (#39)\n\n* stage 1: publish-site report\n\nAudit every EventBus::publish in codeless-runtime production source\nfor the BROWSER-LAUNCHER M5 repo-scoped subscribe filter. Output\nclassifies each call site by event kind, envelope (job_id, stage_id,\ntask_id), and how a fan-out filter can resolve repo_id. Most sites\nresolve via jobs.repo_id; 11 red rows (reviews + scope-patch\napprove/reject + assistant/chat synthetic ids) need either a missing\njob_id on the envelope or an explicit Library classification before\nM5''s filter contract can land.\n\n* stage 0: audit every EventBus::publish call site and produce the publish-site report — list each event kind, whether the published Event already carries a repo_id (or is library-scope), and the call site path:line — output committed as DOCS/EVENT-PUBLISH-AUDIT.md so the REVIEW gate has something concrete to read\n\n* stage 3: add Repo { repo_id } and Library variants to EventFilter\n\nWire-side: `codeless-rpc::EventFilter` gains `Repo { repo_id }` and\n`Library`; `All` is retained (doc-marked as legacy) so the global\nevent-log view and `codeless tail` keep working while every new\nsubscription moves onto the workspace-scoped channels.\n\nRuntime fan-out: `SubscribeFilter::Repo(RepoId)` matches when the\npayload carries `repo_id` (the six library-payload variants + the\nthree `JobQueued` sites identified in `DOCS/EVENT-PUBLISH-AUDIT.md`)\nor when the envelope `job_id` resolves through a snapshot of\n`jobs.repo_id` taken at subscribe time and kept fresh by folding\nincoming `JobQueued` events into the live map. `SubscribeFilter::\nLibrary` is the inverse — events whose `job_id` does not resolve\n(assistant + unbound-chat synthetic ids) plus events with no ids at\nall and no payload repo.\n\nTransports: the in-process router maps the four `EventFilter`\nvariants onto `SubscribeFilter`; the HTTP transport accepts\n`scope=repo&repo_id=…` and `scope=library` on `GET /events`, and the\nclient URL builder mirrors the mapping. The UI''s hand-mirrored\n`EventFilter` and `HttpSseClient.buildSubscribeUrl` are updated in\nthe same change-set so the wire ends are not allowed to drift.\n\nCoverage: `crates/codeless-runtime/tests/event_filter_repo_library.\nrs` drives two `MockRunner`-backed jobs across two repos plus a\nsynthetic-id assistant publish, and asserts that the per-repo and\nlibrary subscribers partition the stream the way M5 requires —\nincluding the live `JobQueued -> job-repo map` armings the\ndownstream runner events depend on.\n\n* stage 2: add Repo { repo_id } and Library variants to EventFilter in codeless-rpc; keep All as deprecated-but-present for the global event log view; update RpcServer::subscribe signature and the in-process + http transports; unit tests cover the filter at the fan-out layer with a MockRunner harness\n\n* stage 4: thread repo_id through the fs.* RPCs (fs_cwd, fs_read_dir, fs_read_file, fs_write_file and any siblings); server resolves repo_id to the attached workspace''s fs_root and uses that as the jail root for the call; reject calls with an unknown or detached repo_id; add a fs_root_for_repo helper on the runtime so future RPCs reuse it\n\n* stage 3: thread repo_id through the fs.* RPCs (fs_cwd, fs_read_dir, fs_read_file, fs_write_file and any siblings); server resolves repo_id to the attached workspace''s fs_root and uses that as the jail root for the call; reject calls with an unknown or detached repo_id; add a fs_root_for_repo helper on the runtime so future RPCs reuse it\n\n* stage 4: server-side scoping — at this point both subscribe and fs.* are workspace-scoped on the wire; confirm the API shape against BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md §\"RPC additions\" and lock it before touching the UI\n\n* stage 6: update the UI''s RpcClient call sites to pass activeRepoId on every subscribe and every fs.* call; open a parallel Library-scope subscription for the workspace picker; the file explorer rehydrates when activeRepoId changes\n\n- methods.ts re-exports the eight server-side fs.* arg/result types\n  from generated/wire so repo_id is in RpcArgs<\"fs_*\">; fs_search and\n  fs_glob keep their hand shape but gain repo_id for parity.\n- fs_cwd RpcMethodMap entry switches to FsCwdArgs.\n- useFileTree / FileExplorer / ExplorerSearch / useDocument /\n  NewEditorDialog / HandoverPanel / RunPane.fs_stat / CwdBreadcrumb /\n  composer / native.ts thread repo_id on every fs.* call. Job-owning\n  panes use job.repo_id; workspace-owning views read activeRepoId\n  from useWorkspacesStore. native.ts reads the store at call time so\n  a workspace switch retargets the next tool call.\n- useFileTree clears its cached nodes/expanded state when repoId\n  changes, so the file explorer rehydrates on a picker switch.\n- useWorkspacesSync flips to { scope: \"library\" } so the picker''s\n  parallel channel is workspace-lifecycle-only.\n- mock client narrows on all four EventFilter variants; library\n  matches envelopes without a job_id, repo matches via a forward-\n  compat cast. Two test doubles in ChatMessageList.test.tsx and\n  ChatTab.test.tsx widen their scope narrowing.\n- App.tsx fs_cwd fallback waits for activeRepoId and passes it\n  through.\n- byte_limit dropped from fs_read_file callers (wire no longer\n  carries it); create_parents dropped from fs_write_file callers.\n\n* stage 5: update the UI''s RpcClient call sites to pass activeRepoId on every subscribe and every fs.* call; open a parallel Library-scope subscription for the workspace picker; the file explorer rehydrates when activeRepoId changes\n\n* stage 7: read ?workspace=<repo_id> from window.location on initial load and pre-populate activeRepoId; call history.replaceState on every setActive so refresh, share-link, and browser-back land on the correct workspace; verify no regression in deep-link behaviour for the existing Tauri webview path\n\n* stage 6: read ?workspace=<repo_id> from window.location on initial load and pre-populate activeRepoId; call history.replaceState on every setActive so refresh, share-link, and browser-back land on the correct workspace; verify no regression in deep-link behaviour for the existing Tauri webview path\n\n* stage 8: per-tab storage audit — grep the Terax-derived UI for localStorage, sessionStorage, and zustand persist; classify each hit as library-level or tab-level; move the tab-level hits (assistant focus thread, open job tabs) to sessionStorage so two browser tabs viewing two attached workspaces no longer leak workbench state across each other; audit committed as DOCS/STORAGE-AUDIT.md\n\n* stage 7: per-tab storage audit — grep the Terax-derived UI for localStorage, sessionStorage, and zustand persist; classify each hit as library-level (shared across tabs is correct) or tab-level (must move to in-memory or sessionStorage); land the moves so cross-tab state leakage does not reintroduce the symptom this job is meant to fix\n\n* stage 10: final cleanup — mark BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md milestones 5, 6 as [x] and 4, 10 as [~] with deviation notes; document the workspace-scoping wire contract in UI-ARCHITECTURE.md so the next reader does not have to walk this job''s commits to recover the model\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* stage 9: final cleanup — update DOCS/UI-ARCHITECTURE.md and BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md to mark milestones 5, 6, 9 as [x], note any deviations from the original scope, and confirm R1/R2/R3 hold (no tokio::process leak, no @tauri-apps imports outside the shell zone, single UI tree)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"264081ca0f50642f3dcb557ede413c3a018d6eac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/264081ca0f50642f3dcb557ede413c3a018d6eac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86","verification":{"payload":"tree 264081ca0f50642f3dcb557ede413c3a018d6eac\nparent ba68b9689f812c0c56b857a7899bbece9cc6c7d2\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1779164533 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779164533 +0700\n\nCodeless/workspace scoping (#39)\n\n* stage 1: publish-site report\n\nAudit every EventBus::publish in codeless-runtime production source\nfor the BROWSER-LAUNCHER M5 repo-scoped subscribe filter. Output\nclassifies each call site by event kind, envelope (job_id, stage_id,\ntask_id), and how a fan-out filter can resolve repo_id. Most sites\nresolve via jobs.repo_id; 11 red rows (reviews + scope-patch\napprove/reject + assistant/chat synthetic ids) need either a missing\njob_id on the envelope or an explicit Library classification before\nM5''s filter contract can land.\n\n* stage 0: audit every EventBus::publish call site and produce the publish-site report — list each event kind, whether the published Event already carries a repo_id (or is library-scope), and the call site path:line — output committed as DOCS/EVENT-PUBLISH-AUDIT.md so the REVIEW gate has something concrete to read\n\n* stage 3: add Repo { repo_id } and Library variants to EventFilter\n\nWire-side: `codeless-rpc::EventFilter` gains `Repo { repo_id }` and\n`Library`; `All` is retained (doc-marked as legacy) so the global\nevent-log view and `codeless tail` keep working while every new\nsubscription moves onto the workspace-scoped channels.\n\nRuntime fan-out: `SubscribeFilter::Repo(RepoId)` matches when the\npayload carries `repo_id` (the six library-payload variants + the\nthree `JobQueued` sites identified in `DOCS/EVENT-PUBLISH-AUDIT.md`)\nor when the envelope `job_id` resolves through a snapshot of\n`jobs.repo_id` taken at subscribe time and kept fresh by folding\nincoming `JobQueued` events into the live map. `SubscribeFilter::\nLibrary` is the inverse — events whose `job_id` does not resolve\n(assistant + unbound-chat synthetic ids) plus events with no ids at\nall and no payload repo.\n\nTransports: the in-process router maps the four `EventFilter`\nvariants onto `SubscribeFilter`; the HTTP transport accepts\n`scope=repo&repo_id=…` and `scope=library` on `GET /events`, and the\nclient URL builder mirrors the mapping. The UI''s hand-mirrored\n`EventFilter` and `HttpSseClient.buildSubscribeUrl` are updated in\nthe same change-set so the wire ends are not allowed to drift.\n\nCoverage: `crates/codeless-runtime/tests/event_filter_repo_library.\nrs` drives two `MockRunner`-backed jobs across two repos plus a\nsynthetic-id assistant publish, and asserts that the per-repo and\nlibrary subscribers partition the stream the way M5 requires —\nincluding the live `JobQueued -> job-repo map` armings the\ndownstream runner events depend on.\n\n* stage 2: add Repo { repo_id } and Library variants to EventFilter in codeless-rpc; keep All as deprecated-but-present for the global event log view; update RpcServer::subscribe signature and the in-process + http transports; unit tests cover the filter at the fan-out layer with a MockRunner harness\n\n* stage 4: thread repo_id through the fs.* RPCs (fs_cwd, fs_read_dir, fs_read_file, fs_write_file and any siblings); server resolves repo_id to the attached workspace''s fs_root and uses that as the jail root for the call; reject calls with an unknown or detached repo_id; add a fs_root_for_repo helper on the runtime so future RPCs reuse it\n\n* stage 3: thread repo_id through the fs.* RPCs (fs_cwd, fs_read_dir, fs_read_file, fs_write_file and any siblings); server resolves repo_id to the attached workspace''s fs_root and uses that as the jail root for the call; reject calls with an unknown or detached repo_id; add a fs_root_for_repo helper on the runtime so future RPCs reuse it\n\n* stage 4: server-side scoping — at this point both subscribe and fs.* are workspace-scoped on the wire; confirm the API shape against BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md §\"RPC additions\" and lock it before touching the UI\n\n* stage 6: update the UI''s RpcClient call sites to pass activeRepoId on every subscribe and every fs.* call; open a parallel Library-scope subscription for the workspace picker; the file explorer rehydrates when activeRepoId changes\n\n- methods.ts re-exports the eight server-side fs.* arg/result types\n  from generated/wire so repo_id is in RpcArgs<\"fs_*\">; fs_search and\n  fs_glob keep their hand shape but gain repo_id for parity.\n- fs_cwd RpcMethodMap entry switches to FsCwdArgs.\n- useFileTree / FileExplorer / ExplorerSearch / useDocument /\n  NewEditorDialog / HandoverPanel / RunPane.fs_stat / CwdBreadcrumb /\n  composer / native.ts thread repo_id on every fs.* call. Job-owning\n  panes use job.repo_id; workspace-owning views read activeRepoId\n  from useWorkspacesStore. native.ts reads the store at call time so\n  a workspace switch retargets the next tool call.\n- useFileTree clears its cached nodes/expanded state when repoId\n  changes, so the file explorer rehydrates on a picker switch.\n- useWorkspacesSync flips to { scope: \"library\" } so the picker''s\n  parallel channel is workspace-lifecycle-only.\n- mock client narrows on all four EventFilter variants; library\n  matches envelopes without a job_id, repo matches via a forward-\n  compat cast. Two test doubles in ChatMessageList.test.tsx and\n  ChatTab.test.tsx widen their scope narrowing.\n- App.tsx fs_cwd fallback waits for activeRepoId and passes it\n  through.\n- byte_limit dropped from fs_read_file callers (wire no longer\n  carries it); create_parents dropped from fs_write_file callers.\n\n* stage 5: update the UI''s RpcClient call sites to pass activeRepoId on every subscribe and every fs.* call; open a parallel Library-scope subscription for the workspace picker; the file explorer rehydrates when activeRepoId changes\n\n* stage 7: read ?workspace=<repo_id> from window.location on initial load and pre-populate activeRepoId; call history.replaceState on every setActive so refresh, share-link, and browser-back land on the correct workspace; verify no regression in deep-link behaviour for the existing Tauri webview path\n\n* stage 6: read ?workspace=<repo_id> from window.location on initial load and pre-populate activeRepoId; call history.replaceState on every setActive so refresh, share-link, and browser-back land on the correct workspace; verify no regression in deep-link behaviour for the existing Tauri webview path\n\n* stage 8: per-tab storage audit — grep the Terax-derived UI for localStorage, sessionStorage, and zustand persist; classify each hit as library-level or tab-level; move the tab-level hits (assistant focus thread, open job tabs) to sessionStorage so two browser tabs viewing two attached workspaces no longer leak workbench state across each other; audit committed as DOCS/STORAGE-AUDIT.md\n\n* stage 7: per-tab storage audit — grep the Terax-derived UI for localStorage, sessionStorage, and zustand persist; classify each hit as library-level (shared across tabs is correct) or tab-level (must move to in-memory or sessionStorage); land the moves so cross-tab state leakage does not reintroduce the symptom this job is meant to fix\n\n* stage 10: final cleanup — mark BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md milestones 5, 6 as [x] and 4, 10 as [~] with deviation notes; document the workspace-scoping wire contract in UI-ARCHITECTURE.md so the next reader does not have to walk this job''s commits to recover the model\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* stage 9: final cleanup — update DOCS/UI-ARCHITECTURE.md and BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md to mark milestones 5, 6, 9 as [x], note any deviations from the original scope, and confirm R1/R2/R3 hold (no tokio::process leak, no @tauri-apps imports outside the shell zone, single UI tree)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqC+V1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvTMQAJUntEodB3gBrFew9YiSpTJm\nQRjYrOG6cPNrSRTELe776hc4rrqjva3WyB/SOisQdV860WXybQSDLFkpEYG61KeN\nCfzPhEIW8ZDPCg67JUqWeSeW4VXtLpPc/mbsUJkys0e2o+81Tvr8mNrdon8B+IQK\nUq68Lxz/RE+KdDbu/nhZ1Ai8R784NvQ3JUfEr65AJxxvBGwmv2V1ZTQIhik7p5wr\nLG7smgfYDxy2yS8xc/TQz2n2olKOI+U5V38vZfSEhia4Q8X1sq5l0SfW7dY2UiD7\nzZAV9MZKQO55OJO2UMPide+3acd0dluzcx5wA0dtbGZQXRqARb6qq+Pho7JO/50Y\ncUuNaPYkd0TLv2E6Wso8sBpm/52K94blft45L/gkPzaT6GBA0dFadwztbm0w5nBc\nO7gE657mpLCY56c7LEQ92X5tfS7ilK+/Eb/aJVEgCuAB58x/rOtSE9StlOCyilhK\n62KUMS3VR7yqjT13zLtdL96nRzx2RHkUjGWUucCofDDopqN6Od7Z0CE+ndWI6erD\nDLbrSlfwWym0l0bwUtV8n2SxCGsfFyQQCAmCYyrFXI3ZYEluKIz8SGgKcipEqCQt\nG8iIZmcZaub92/eHS36rYcxxL+XOsiDkvNpxhJgcr4vGusLdmxdBRWC3awqAzn3z\n1OUsu7++fqXiPcsf6kmB\n=8Fq7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T04:22:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86","node_id":"C_kwDOSa1B6doAKDJlNDBmZjhiNjFiZDQ3OWIwM2JlODMwYzE1NTAwYzI4ZjNhMzBlODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/ba68b9689f812c0c56b857a7899bbece9cc6c7d2","sha":"ba68b9689f812c0c56b857a7899bbece9cc6c7d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/ba68b9689f812c0c56b857a7899bbece9cc6c7d2"}],"sha":"2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/2e40ff8b61bd479b03be830c15500c28f3a30e86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/ba68b9689f812c0c56b857a7899bbece9cc6c7d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T04:16:38Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T04:16:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(runtime): per-stage Git rail actually pushes after commit (#38)\n\nThe Git trio row''s label promises \"commit + push\" but the\nimplementation was commit-only — `commit_stage_changes` shelled out to\n`commit_all_changes` and never pushed, so stages succeeded locally\nwhile remaining invisible on the remote. Operators watching a job on\nGitHub saw nothing until manual intervention.\n\nAdd `push_current_branch` to `codeless-adapters-host` (runs\n`git push -u origin HEAD`, idempotent across stages), call it from\n`commit_stage_changes` after a successful commit, and route a push\nfailure through the same `Failed` rail status as a commit failure so\nthe operator sees the git stderr in `failure_detail`. The no-diff\n`Skipped` case stays a no-op — nothing to commit, nothing to push.\n\nTests: push lands a commit on a bare-repo origin and is idempotent on\na second call; push without a configured remote returns the typed\npush-op error; the trio emitter flips the Git rail to Failed when the\npush step fails post-commit (regression pin for this fix).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc60274629b4544aa7031bf919ee3f8274c6d806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/fc60274629b4544aa7031bf919ee3f8274c6d806"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/ba68b9689f812c0c56b857a7899bbece9cc6c7d2","verification":{"payload":"tree fc60274629b4544aa7031bf919ee3f8274c6d806\nparent a138caed57e38d7c59a3cb4b7ba28cb47f01645e\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1779164198 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779164198 +0700\n\nfix(runtime): per-stage Git rail actually pushes after commit (#38)\n\nThe Git trio row''s label promises \"commit + push\" but the\nimplementation was commit-only — `commit_stage_changes` shelled out to\n`commit_all_changes` and never pushed, so stages succeeded locally\nwhile remaining invisible on the remote. Operators watching a job on\nGitHub saw nothing until manual intervention.\n\nAdd `push_current_branch` to `codeless-adapters-host` (runs\n`git push -u origin HEAD`, idempotent across stages), call it from\n`commit_stage_changes` after a successful commit, and route a push\nfailure through the same `Failed` rail status as a commit failure so\nthe operator sees the git stderr in `failure_detail`. The no-diff\n`Skipped` case stays a no-op — nothing to commit, nothing to push.\n\nTests: push lands a commit on a bare-repo origin and is idempotent on\na second call; push without a configured remote returns the typed\npush-op error; the trio emitter flips the Git rail to Failed when the\npush step fails post-commit (regression pin for this fix).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqC+QmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/n0QAHCCmCDPbBh3oY8hXHYaYvJ+\nBoKdt21uoMWStuIuczfh6zqE229/SFNCgPmMp8V6KKNPGDlzme//Rid7dzewC8If\n0Ov0Y02y+zr0q9bTBU/a3UZFQ7zJbmjMg0GRWDtv+ohXaClxEGomphLvE1Pqxo7Z\n6VA/8OpFAKBU3Ewj3wNWryZBFmGTElDSaL2WPPydtqvRcKI38CsyAQRLQKbXUoYB\nc0VKww6DeaAjypV1q6J2UqgKKuwnMrrLz02mHbRx3oeb7mtWlJiFT054eU/honyN\nrzCOPe2Xko45wya/pMVq6PQm+OV4cRNbORAMcaQOGC/R57ACEQH3U00YrqWf2URz\nExZfLqcQcnWbMIzzW6hkJWQMIc3bSKYvq1J3/5n0YTrPjp6VmhyJ2SN3m/mOSphu\nyOnX0bgS1CgK4Bd1CIjXEr6pvEFfmfovJK4/CpEXvjeQ7nCVOX1NNwooTibJ/mwM\n71th3fKWTlYqPNOJ+kLjVdmoBFKbziDgiRN4ki6QVRB83KANvTlh5cX3m/Kb5Ii8\niG9B5n9xCKtQijY+S+fvf/mwEFDTm/TSaP80D9TDHRP79t0/ZDKUC9Vu+7palpsP\nJztSw1pMsP30tqlbiULhBe7TKaOcFlAzg5DUo+uCzHYBI4G2GnVq+JhwTyoxp6Y6\nHcr+jWXfSnNnhBhsoOSX\n=eO5y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T04:16:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/ba68b9689f812c0c56b857a7899bbece9cc6c7d2","node_id":"C_kwDOSa1B6doAKGJhNjhiOTY4OWY4MTJjMGM1NmI4NTdhNzg5OWJiZWNlOWNjNmM3ZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/a138caed57e38d7c59a3cb4b7ba28cb47f01645e","sha":"a138caed57e38d7c59a3cb4b7ba28cb47f01645e","url":"https://api.g