:"scaffold job: workspace-scoping","tree":{"sha":"f526732d91e2b8bfdc78df2360f86e705b92e794","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/f526732d91e2b8bfdc78df2360f86e705b92e794"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/45a00135299a0821bb89c749f396a5a96ad631eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/45a00135299a0821bb89c749f396a5a96ad631eb","node_id":"C_kwDOSa1B6doAKDQ1YTAwMTM1Mjk5YTA4MjFiYjg5Yzc0OWYzOTZhNWE5NmFkNjMxZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/a2490b15b5dfe53bc6a4022677859f6af98aad94","sha":"a2490b15b5dfe53bc6a4022677859f6af98aad94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/a2490b15b5dfe53bc6a4022677859f6af98aad94"}],"sha":"45a00135299a0821bb89c749f396a5a96ad631eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/45a00135299a0821bb89c749f396a5a96ad631eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/a2490b15b5dfe53bc6a4022677859f6af98aad94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T02:09:33Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T02:09:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"worktree-fs-jail: register worktree base with HostFs so agent_chat works (#37)\n\n* stage 1: confirm reproduction and lock the fix shape\n\nRecord stage-1 recon for the worktree-fs-jail job:\n\n- codeless-cli/src/serve.rs already has the host_fs.add_root call\n  for worktree_root_effective at lines 413-422 (worktree_root_effective\n  bound at line 368); stage 2 has no edit here, but the regression\n  test must still pin the contract.\n- codeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs is NOT patched. Insertion point\n  is between line 160 (end of attached_workspaces rehydration match)\n  and line 163 (runtime.with_fs(Arc::new(host_fs))). paths.worktree_base\n  is in scope from line 134 and create_dir_all''d at line 129, so the\n  HostFs::add_root precondition is met without reordering.\n- HostFs::add_root requires the directory to exist (canonicalise_root\n  at fs.rs:369-375 returns FsError::BadRoot otherwise); both hosts\n  already create_dir_all the worktree base before the registration\n  would run.\n- Reject string lives at codeless-runtime/src/rpc/chat.rs:76.\n- BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md does not contain the ''Known issues - Worktree\n  root is not in the fs jail'' section that SCOPE.md cross-references;\n  stage 4 must either add it (and flip to fixed) or drop the\n  reference.\n\n* stage 0: stage 1 — confirm reproduction and lock the fix shape: re-read BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md ''Known issues — Worktree root is not in the fs jail'', verify the symptom against the running server (open a job''s chat panel; observe the exact ''invalid_argument: agent_chat cwd is outside the configured fs roots'' rejection), grep the two call sites named in the doc (codeless-cli/src/serve.rs ~line 413 after the attached_workspaces rehydration block, and codeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs after its rehydration loop and before with_fs), record the exact line numbers as they exist on this branch in the handover so stage 2 is mechanical\n\n* stage 2: land the fix in both hosts\n\ncodeless-cli/src/serve.rs already registers worktree_root_effective\nwith host_fs via add_root (lines 413-422), so only the desktop host\nneeded the matching call. Add host_fs.add_root(&worktree_base) in\ncodeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs between the attached_workspaces\nrehydration loop and the runtime.with_fs() wrap, surfacing failures\nas BootError::FsRoot the same way HostFs::new errors do. The\ncreate_dir_all(&worktree_base) earlier in boot() guarantees the\ndirectory exists, which add_root requires for canonicalisation.\n\nWithout this, opening the per-job chat panel for any job whose\nworktree lives under ~/.codeless/workspaces/<slug>/worktrees/ is\nrejected by the agent_chat RPC with \"cwd is outside the configured\nfs roots\", because the worktree base sits outside the workspace\nroot that seeds HostFs.\n\n* stage 1: stage 2 — land the fix in both hosts: add host_fs.add_root(&worktree_base) (or the equivalent for the CLI''s worktree_root_effective) to both serve.rs and boot.rs, after std::fs::create_dir_all guarantees the directory exists and before the runtime is wrapped with the host_fs; both hosts share the same fix shape; surface FsRoot errors the same way the surrounding code already does (BootError::FsRoot in boot.rs, anyhow context in serve.rs); no drive-by refactors of either function\n\n* stage 3: regression tests for worktree-root fs jail\n\nUnit test in codeless-adapters-host pins the HostFs shape the boot\nfix relies on: construct against a workspace dir, `add_root` a\nseparate worktree base, then `is_path_allowed` returns true for a\ndescendant of the added root and false for a sibling directory next\nto it. This is exactly the check `agent_chat` performs against a\nper-call `cwd` override, so the test fails the moment a future\nrefactor breaks containment for additional roots.\n\nIntegration test in codeless-cli boots `codeless serve` with\n`--fs-root <repo>` and `--worktree-root <wt>`, submits a mock job\nto drive the worktree onto disk, then POSTs `agent_chat` with\n`cwd` set to that worktree path and asserts the response is not\nthe `cwd is outside the configured fs roots` rejection. The wire\nid `claude` passes `parse_cli_runner_id` regardless of whether\nthe binary is installed; the rejection we''re guarding fires\nbefore the runner spawn, so the test is deterministic on any\nhost.\n\n* stage 2: stage 3 — regression test in codeless-adapters-host or codeless-runtime: a unit test that constructs a HostFs, adds a worktree root, and asserts is_path_allowed returns true for a path under it and false for a sibling; plus an integration test (in codeless-cli or codeless-tauri-desktop, whichever already has a boot-level integration harness) that boots a runtime, submits a no-op job that creates a worktree, then calls agent_chat with cwd set to that worktree path and asserts the call does not return InvalidArgument with the fs-roots message\n\n* stage 4 — close out: author Known issues section in BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md\n\nThe §\"Known issues — Worktree root is not in the fs jail\" section\nreferenced by the job SCOPE.md did not exist in BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md\non this branch (confirmed in stages 1 and 2 handovers). Author it\nin its post-fix form: Status: fixed in 168cb7f, with the actual\nline ranges of the two host registrations under the \"Where it\nbites\" bullet — codeless-cli/src/serve.rs:413-422 (pre-existing)\nand codeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs:161-169 (added in 168cb7f).\nThe section is kept so future readers understand why both hosts\nregister the worktree base with HostFs at boot.\n\n* stage 3: stage 4 — close out: flip the ''Status: open'' line in BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md §''Known issues — Worktree root is not in the fs jail'' to ''Status: fixed in <commit-sha>''; record under the existing ''Where it bites'' bullet the line ranges actually changed in serve.rs and boot.rs; do not delete the section (it documents history for the next reader)","tree":{"sha":"f781d39c96d9da89348c1aec6a56217d2dc698ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/f781d39c96d9da89348c1aec6a56217d2dc698ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/a2490b15b5dfe53bc6a4022677859f6af98aad94","verification":{"payload":"tree f781d39c96d9da89348c1aec6a56217d2dc698ea\nparent 6a2541c8e7c95712bff56e7ad64b07b8bbb8a1c2\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1779156573 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779156573 +0700\n\nworktree-fs-jail: register worktree base with HostFs so agent_chat works (#37)\n\n* stage 1: confirm reproduction and lock the fix shape\n\nRecord stage-1 recon for the worktree-fs-jail job:\n\n- codeless-cli/src/serve.rs already has the host_fs.add_root call\n  for worktree_root_effective at lines 413-422 (worktree_root_effective\n  bound at line 368); stage 2 has no edit here, but the regression\n  test must still pin the contract.\n- codeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs is NOT patched. Insertion point\n  is between line 160 (end of attached_workspaces rehydration match)\n  and line 163 (runtime.with_fs(Arc::new(host_fs))). paths.worktree_base\n  is in scope from line 134 and create_dir_all''d at line 129, so the\n  HostFs::add_root precondition is met without reordering.\n- HostFs::add_root requires the directory to exist (canonicalise_root\n  at fs.rs:369-375 returns FsError::BadRoot otherwise); both hosts\n  already create_dir_all the worktree base before the registration\n  would run.\n- Reject string lives at codeless-runtime/src/rpc/chat.rs:76.\n- BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md does not contain the ''Known issues - Worktree\n  root is not in the fs jail'' section that SCOPE.md cross-references;\n  stage 4 must either add it (and flip to fixed) or drop the\n  reference.\n\n* stage 0: stage 1 — confirm reproduction and lock the fix shape: re-read BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md ''Known issues — Worktree root is not in the fs jail'', verify the symptom against the running server (open a job''s chat panel; observe the exact ''invalid_argument: agent_chat cwd is outside the configured fs roots'' rejection), grep the two call sites named in the doc (codeless-cli/src/serve.rs ~line 413 after the attached_workspaces rehydration block, and codeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs after its rehydration loop and before with_fs), record the exact line numbers as they exist on this branch in the handover so stage 2 is mechanical\n\n* stage 2: land the fix in both hosts\n\ncodeless-cli/src/serve.rs already registers worktree_root_effective\nwith host_fs via add_root (lines 413-422), so only the desktop host\nneeded the matching call. Add host_fs.add_root(&worktree_base) in\ncodeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs between the attached_workspaces\nrehydration loop and the runtime.with_fs() wrap, surfacing failures\nas BootError::FsRoot the same way HostFs::new errors do. The\ncreate_dir_all(&worktree_base) earlier in boot() guarantees the\ndirectory exists, which add_root requires for canonicalisation.\n\nWithout this, opening the per-job chat panel for any job whose\nworktree lives under ~/.codeless/workspaces/<slug>/worktrees/ is\nrejected by the agent_chat RPC with \"cwd is outside the configured\nfs roots\", because the worktree base sits outside the workspace\nroot that seeds HostFs.\n\n* stage 1: stage 2 — land the fix in both hosts: add host_fs.add_root(&worktree_base) (or the equivalent for the CLI''s worktree_root_effective) to both serve.rs and boot.rs, after std::fs::create_dir_all guarantees the directory exists and before the runtime is wrapped with the host_fs; both hosts share the same fix shape; surface FsRoot errors the same way the surrounding code already does (BootError::FsRoot in boot.rs, anyhow context in serve.rs); no drive-by refactors of either function\n\n* stage 3: regression tests for worktree-root fs jail\n\nUnit test in codeless-adapters-host pins the HostFs shape the boot\nfix relies on: construct against a workspace dir, `add_root` a\nseparate worktree base, then `is_path_allowed` returns true for a\ndescendant of the added root and false for a sibling directory next\nto it. This is exactly the check `agent_chat` performs against a\nper-call `cwd` override, so the test fails the moment a future\nrefactor breaks containment for additional roots.\n\nIntegration test in codeless-cli boots `codeless serve` with\n`--fs-root <repo>` and `--worktree-root <wt>`, submits a mock job\nto drive the worktree onto disk, then POSTs `agent_chat` with\n`cwd` set to that worktree path and asserts the response is not\nthe `cwd is outside the configured fs roots` rejection. The wire\nid `claude` passes `parse_cli_runner_id` regardless of whether\nthe binary is installed; the rejection we''re guarding fires\nbefore the runner spawn, so the test is deterministic on any\nhost.\n\n* stage 2: stage 3 — regression test in codeless-adapters-host or codeless-runtime: a unit test that constructs a HostFs, adds a worktree root, and asserts is_path_allowed returns true for a path under it and false for a sibling; plus an integration test (in codeless-cli or codeless-tauri-desktop, whichever already has a boot-level integration harness) that boots a runtime, submits a no-op job that creates a worktree, then calls agent_chat with cwd set to that worktree path and asserts the call does not return InvalidArgument with the fs-roots message\n\n* stage 4 — close out: author Known issues section in BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md\n\nThe §\"Known issues — Worktree root is not in the fs jail\" section\nreferenced by the job SCOPE.md did not exist in BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md\non this branch (confirmed in stages 1 and 2 handovers). Author it\nin its post-fix form: Status: fixed in 168cb7f, with the actual\nline ranges of the two host registrations under the \"Where it\nbites\" bullet — codeless-cli/src/serve.rs:413-422 (pre-existing)\nand codeless-tauri-desktop/src/boot.rs:161-169 (added in 168cb7f).\nThe section is kept so future readers understand why both hosts\nregister the worktree base with HostFs at boot.\n\n* stage 3: stage 4 — close out: flip the ''Status: open'' line in BROWSER-LAUNCHER.md §''Known issues — Worktree root is not in the fs jail'' to ''Status: fixed in <commit-sha>''; record under the existing ''Where it bites'' bullet the line ranges actually changed in serve.rs and boot.rs; do not delete the section (it documents history for the next reader)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqC8ZdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATAIQAHqP4djvVMfyW6/4Jq2kZwlM\nzjJjiRHlTSwFUMJHDRc3x+6V1Ym/j8JBWnTs/4QRihaX3UIbpD7BiAvwVEKxAoWG\nLoIFo+Crqud1dCcM+Fd/ivJWZjOXtUvGSdK/gsrzCzA4+fS/BQGXJYbX+GkLbqlo\n9QmgcPoLo1TVknLxiDtFjx6Fet8SucrsXBEEfXXk2NhQ+AyXSE3xtWvWyRaQ1c86\nX+WbnK1jFAj1VrgONnn+u8OqpP3LZXa7pwVZmVg3kqNSHFmBi6bXcbKCjznbEK9Q\nfG1MAhx3eceRFZrkvIi6jHuQ6fHM8H9pNbpU2N3t6AHTTNE0QblEj9RV0X