s://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/ff5aad7feb22986a8db0aef24e243b6ed980c5aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:16:49Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:16:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(trio-gate): route Failed/timeout to auto-bypass + surface rail reason (#31)\n\nJob 01KRX4ZPF... ran for ~110 min on a failed `docs` trio row because\nthe closing-trio gate''s `trio_resolved -> bool` treated `Failed` as\n\"not resolved\" and polled forever, defeating `auto_bypass_policy =\nlong-term`.\n\nLong-term fixes:\n\n- Tri-state gate: `TrioGateOutcome { Resolved | Pending | Failed }`.\n  Failed rails surface a per-rail reason from a new\n  `todos.failure_detail` column (migration 0023) so the gate can\n  produce `StageCompleted { Failed }` with real context.\n- 5-min max-wait + 10s heartbeat (`StageTrioGateWaiting`) so a wedged\n  resolver becomes a stage failure, not a silent hang. UI now shows\n  \"waiting on: docs, git\" instead of an apparently-running stage.\n- `Failed` and `TimedOut` route through the existing stage-failure\n  path -> `try_auto_bypass`, so policy-configured jobs advance and\n  unconfigured jobs halt with a real reason on the stage row.\n- `Event::TodoCompleted` gains `failure_detail: Option<String>`;\n  emitters thread real strings (handover IO error, verify exit code,\n  git commit error). UI renders the rail''s reason inline under the\n  failing row.\n\nRegression test `failed_trio_row_routes_stage_to_failed_with_detail`\nrecreates the original failure end-to-end through the recorder +\nbus and asserts the stage now fails with the rail''s reason.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c0fc3bc73b732f6c7127348da609d81f7d74dc15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/c0fc3bc73b732f6c7127348da609d81f7d74dc15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/ff5aad7feb22986a8db0aef24e243b6ed980c5aa","verification":{"payload":"tree c0fc3bc73b732f6c7127348da609d81f7d74dc15\nparent d268d2ba862854cd41f74f03829dc7d71f9fcc43\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1779106609 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779106609 +0700\n\nfix(trio-gate): route Failed/timeout to auto-bypass + surface rail reason (#31)\n\nJob 01KRX4ZPF... ran for ~110 min on a failed `docs` trio row because\nthe closing-trio gate''s `trio_resolved -> bool` treated `Failed` as\n\"not resolved\" and polled forever, defeating `auto_bypass_policy =\nlong-term`.\n\nLong-term fixes:\n\n- Tri-state gate: `TrioGateOutcome { Resolved | Pending | Failed }`.\n  Failed rails surface a per-rail reason from a new\n  `todos.failure_detail` column (migration 0023) so the gate can\n  produce `StageCompleted { Failed }` with real context.\n- 5-min max-wait + 10s heartbeat (`StageTrioGateWaiting`) so a wedged\n  resolver becomes a stage failure, not a silent hang. UI now shows\n  \"waiting on: docs, git\" instead of an apparently-running stage.\n- `Failed` and `TimedOut` route through the existing stage-failure\n  path -> `try_auto_bypass`, so policy-configured jobs advance and\n  unconfigured jobs halt with a real reason on the stage row.\n- `Event::TodoCompleted` gains `failure_detail: Option<String>`;\n  emitters thread real strings (handover IO error, verify exit code,\n  git commit error). UI renders the rail''s reason inline under the\n  failing row.\n\nRegression test `failed_trio_row_routes_stage_to_failed_with_detail`\nrecreates the original failure end-to-end through the recorder +\nbus and asserts the stage now fails with the rail''s reason.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCwMxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGDkQAEeqxc+FzWjSmNrw07JeGXPp\nup6kApr6CpKgpjTsh/ImmY5D7pAuwLQvrzeIQ7TnIFZ6wes+8Yy+jZhZpicGtD31\nPiyeFdVfhBG8cUroPikqcflCNQruxScO8jmcQHHv/AfbJChx5/JMJsg/9DARq2jr\nibnUswz8yuzgjQeUHHPvgPwPb1dwPNCxrxiEQsGBnr3ydT9zYcj/umbS1a13d6NT\nQiaX9juGCXb9baKVbAv/MUvqjmpAwea17KdFPUt72yIXeZLm6/JcUXGiVzRGed8q\ngBkFfWOP8Ze+CI+bkipvo4lmrifNPcX8Rv5Yl2irmXGyO7gmn0LZn5DmpvnqRL2+\nsr27HpcF91H6NmKgD82jZdJnb1YOXQimWX7DLaw8bOkaO77e5HNCrDni14Hf0dy+\nBO1IMtNDVDE5G2aoVkNre+PMVCXbSdRbsOuW9AjEqK+jX/Zes2ty3Pmjhrq5fCKM\nLuUqMTmChh3G9SW+cI+KeUZo1tNDGsY3YLML/RbURU59yWExvRdKZa6bxa3OJj9r\nV+BSnj4kAZWBwJBSE0meE5anrGshDeCWSqj+SyUxiZbWesgp6m3UNxdYV8t7sME9\n0kbI/UFsYSrqAbYhDwlfvpEDNbUTWYHHxrD+ITS+K0VPh92xtY30yV4NO8lJk6kG\nUT08U33qr5cOZAoSJkWp\n=1IHQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-18T12:16:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/ff5aad7feb22986a8db0aef24e243b6ed980c5aa","node_id":"C_kwDOSa1B6doAKGZmNWFhZDdmZWIyMjk4NmE4ZGIwYWVmMjRlMjQzYjZlZDk4MGM1YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev/codeless/commit/d268d2ba862854cd41f74f03829dc7d71f9fcc43","sha":"d268d2ba862854cd41f74f03829dc7d71f9fcc43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/d268d2ba862854cd41f74f03829dc7d71f9fcc43"}],"sha":"ff5aad7feb22986a8db0aef24e243b6ed980c5aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/ff5aad7feb22986a8db0aef24e243b6ed980c5aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev","id":18637436,"login":"NubeDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjM3NDM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/d268d2ba862854cd41f74f03829dc7d71f9fcc43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:16:38Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"Aidan P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:16:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add JOB-CHAT (per-Job chat substrate + supervisor) + cross-ref from JOB-WORKFLOW (#32)\n\nJOB-CHAT.md specifies the conversational counterpart to JOB-WORKFLOW:\none chat thread per Job shared across web / Telegram / Slack, plus a\nper-Run supervisor agent that watches the run and replies in that\nthread. JOB-WORKFLOW gets a paragraph pointing at it so the\niterate-loop vs. conversation-loop split is visible from both sides.\n\nNo code changes; docs-only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a27710c22b22804e0883aa8e1f25931089bba133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/a27710c22b22804e0883aa8e1f25931089bba133"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/d268d2ba862854cd41f74f03829dc7d71f9fcc43","verification":{"payload":"tree a27710c22b22804e0883aa8e1f25931089bba133\nparent f0bddc8f4af4d720ed58b2f041ccb609cb893a15\nauthor Aidan P <aidan@enviroservices.com.au> 1779106598 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779106598 +0700\n\ndocs: add JOB-CHAT (per-Job chat substrate + supervisor) + cross-ref from JOB-WORKFLOW (#32)\n\nJOB-CHAT.md specifies the conversational counterpart to JOB-WORKFLOW:\none chat thread per Job shared across web / Telegram / Slack, plus a\nper-Run supervisor agent that watches the run and replies in that\nthread. JOB-WORKFLOW gets a paragraph pointing at it so the\niterate-loop vs. conversation-loop split is visible from both sides.\n\nNo code changes; docs-only.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCwMmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALGkQABmF9F5/DUv2Fspy1LJ2jJL2\nvz/RyUf+xuAsArl5HroWQBwWl68aIqEDgE5Citja2kkWTq/AsT1NiT3KieDQ6Lry\nHU1D8Luyl4jtK6V4ABMbTdvUWUu1PhTYCvr1JTtqFY2zF5STpxJEp2olrlabds92\nANX2o+/6eDUl4BuPz6/NLupoQ322WQT/+JiDlsQOjmzUgjtFCmVAw8KytFfWsxh4\nO2jsDv2zg9BBJm94TXGPaqySv4qrHg3HLqeVD5jhva5BSCmOsptaD8euta2MpEj7\niUBN3ms3D0sm0RoAKcuiEt/aruuBr8mPB42B51n0h/L9QloNYMi7i0eMJXvePPlT\n4eyk7UxYdQWxQvp53eysw4XTC2qIY5g8hT9gRoMwG0mCPDUOnKxJEEPcEXoOiQta\nQOrJ+2gFye57/7C/eH2MmBoiVwzlbAPfLovZ18plgw31Zs8lreQlOGZ4rV9tu6Gw\nl8+rcQmlsGFOnufAN/eYqV3sl856J3+OaB9jT18rvTRqVxKKgGbetwmwz+xf3EQa\n6a