/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/commits/a1689f23b8414443ddc202b6b580c653543f281a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T05:23:29Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T05:23:29Z","email":"aidan@enviroservices.com.au","name":"NubeDev"},"message":"M3c: add PathPicker shell capability with browser and Tauri injectors\n\nIntroduces the only legitimately shell-divergent piece of the\nworkspace-attach flow as a capability adapter. Browser injector\nuses showDirectoryPicker() where available and falls back to a\ntyped-input prompt; desktop injector uses @tauri-apps/plugin-dialog\nopen({directory:true}). Both return a non-canonicalised path that\ncallers hand to validate_workspace_path for trust.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ccf1cfd8579c0b1d10df380330147736332c7c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/trees/9ccf1cfd8579c0b1d10df380330147736332c7c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NubeDev/codeless/git/commits/a1689f23b8414443ddc202b6b580c653543f281a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18637436?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NubeDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NubeDev