ite_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-openrouter-companion/commits/d64472c799c9db4d2697e4abc129d82a20b3fd12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T03:36:11Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"NearlCrews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T03:36:11Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"NearlCrews"},"message":"fix(schema): rebuild cron preset arrays per analyzer node\n\ncronPatternSchema returned the shared CRON_PRESET_VALUES and CRON_PRESET_TITLES module arrays when the default was already a preset, so the same enum and enumNames object appeared in every analyzer''s cron node. The SignalK plugin packaging check walks the schema with one seen-set and reports any object seen twice as a circular reference, which failed the App Store compliance gate. A running server was unaffected because the schema still serialized correctly. Build a fresh array per call again, and add a test that walks the schema for shared references.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"587ea2fc0521f02d719852b193d152a7460e5b47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-openrouter-companion/git/trees/587ea2fc0521f02d719852b193d152a7460e5b47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-openrouter-companion/git/commits/d64472c799c9db4d2697e4abc129d82a20b3fd12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","f