https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9","sha":"4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9"}],"sha":"9c4cc01f2fed5bb3efae028d9a8bddc21a6cb6d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/9c4cc01f2fed5bb3efae028d9a8bddc21a6cb6d2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:24:19Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:24:19Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Update low-priority references for 2026 tooling and platforms\n\n- Frameworks: Angular 19-22 (standalone/zoneless defaults, signals,\n  rxjs-interop import fix), Vue 3.5/3.6 status, React Native New\n  Architecture and modern Expo, Flutter Impeller and Riverpod 3,\n  SwiftUI @Observable, Swift 6 concurrency, Kotlin 2 / KMP\n- Languages: current-version boxes for Python, Java, Go, Rust, C#, PHP,\n  Ruby and C++; uv/Ruff and free-threaded Python\n- AI: current Claude models, computer toolset rewrite, Stagehand v4,\n  structured outputs, no hard-coded API keys\n- Infra: Kafka 4 KRaft, RabbitMQ 4 quorum queues, Artifact Registry and\n  Cloud Run functions, App Mesh and Amazon Linux 2 end of support,\n  Module Federation beyond webpack, Turbo cache path\n- Accessibility: 2024-25 legal deadlines, WCAG 2.2, native <dialog>\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01442a389469583c2a56e8994a564a95146c6fa1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/01442a389469583c2a56e8994a564a95146c6fa1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDRmMjc5YTQyZDBjOGFhNzMyZGQwZmZiZTQzODU4MDA4YjljMjhlYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635","sha":"8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635"}],"sha":"4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/4f279a42d0c8aa732dd0ffbe43858008b9c28ea9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:31:29Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:31:29Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Update medium-priority references for 2026 tooling and models\n\n- Next.js: rewrite for Next 16 — uncached fetch by default, async params,\n  ''use cache'' / Cache Components, proxy.ts, Turbopack; fix redirect()\n  inside try/catch advice and the useActionState action signature\n- AI: current models and APIs, structured outputs, Files API; fix made-up\n  Braintrust scorers, deprecated OpenTelemetry package and metric label\n  cardinality; correct fine-tuning memory figures, TRL options, add\n  preference/reinforcement fine-tuning and distillation\n- Build tools: Vite 8 with Rolldown (rolldownOptions, codeSplitting),\n  Rspack, 2026 tooling landscape; Tailwind v4; React Router v7/v8\n- GraphQL: Apollo Server 5 and Client 4 imports, graphql-subscriptions v3\n- Infra: Node 24 images, Compose without version key, current GitHub\n  Actions, External Secrets v1, ingress-nginx retirement and Gateway API\n- Redis licensing/Valkey and node-redis; Prisma 7 setup in NestJS;\n  INP replacing FID; Safari storage eviction note\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55b4ae69002b1e5fc9022a5241e6ac140744618a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/55b4ae69002b1e5fc9022a5241e6ac140744618a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDhjMDRlYjNmMjU5MTBlNGY5ZjI5MDFmNzhkODQ2YzhmZTFmYWQ2MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742","sha":"ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742"}],"sha":"8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/8c04eb3f25910e4f9f2901f78d846c8fe1fad635"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:04:38Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:04:38Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Update high-priority references for 2026 tooling and models\n\nBring the high-priority study notes up to date and fix examples that\nwould not work as written:\n\n- AI: current Claude/OpenAI/open-weight models and prices; LangChain v1,\n  AI SDK v7, Claude Agent SDK and Mem0 APIs; effort replaces temperature\n  on current reasoning models; structured outputs replace forced tools\n- React: React 19 and React Compiler section; ref as a prop; fix\n  parenthesised ''use client'' directives (a no-op) and split the blocks\n  so Prettier keeps them; fix a use() example that suspends forever\n- Next.js 15-16: uncached fetch by default, async params, ''use cache'',\n  proxy.ts; React Router v7/v8; Tailwind v4; ESLint flat config\n- TypeScript 6/7 defaults and deprecations; Express 5 changes and the\n  express-mongo-sanitize incompatibility; modern Node built-ins and LTS\n- Infra: Node 24 images, Compose without version key, Karpenter and\n  External Secrets v1 APIs, GitHub Actions v7\n- Fix quantisation memory figures, a non-expanding Docker CMD variable,\n  and an `eval` identifier in strict-mode code\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"639eb170918abbc9e1a1d2f124b91a4e2c08e57c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/639eb170918abbc9e1a1d2f124b91a4e2c08e57c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKGViZmMyZmZjNWNkOWQ2MGEyZDBjMjM3M2MwODIwMWUzYzEyYmM3NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e","sha":"619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e"}],"sha":"ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/ebfc2ffc5cd9d60a2d0c2373c08201e3c12bc742"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:53:50Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:53:50Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add browser compatibility reference — engines, quirks, desktop vs mobile\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"98264ea66d0d97f314dfbccbe27d9cf7ecb6662f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/98264ea66d0d97f314dfbccbe27d9cf7ecb6662f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDYxOWRkZmE5OWZkYWIxOWQ0OTMyODE2YWE4ZGY2OWU5YWYxMTJmOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69","sha":"01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69"}],"sha":"619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/619ddfa99fdab19d4932816aa8df69e9af112f8e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:23:08Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:23:08Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Modernise PDF reference — standards, embedded files, library status\n\nAdds two sections and reworks the library guidance after checking the\ncurrent state of the ecosystem:\n\n- New section on PDF versions and conformance standards: the version\n  history, why PDF 2.0 is backwards compatible with 1.7, and PDF/A,\n  PDF/UA and PDF/X, which constrain tool choice more than the version\n  number does.\n- New section on embedded files, data and media: the /EmbeddedFiles\n  name tree and /AF associated files, hybrid e-invoicing with\n  Factur-X and ZUGFeRD on PDF/A-3, XMP metadata, and an honest account\n  of embedded audio and video, which plays in Acrobat and almost\n  nowhere else.\n- Library section rewritten around maintenance status. pdf-lib is\n  archived and pdf-parse unmaintained, so code samples now use a\n  maintained pdf-lib fork and unpdf. Also flags wkhtmltopdf as dead\n  and adds EmbedPDF as a PDFium-based rendering alternative.\n- Explains the two-step page lookup: the page tree maps page number to\n  object number, xref maps object number to byte offset.\n- Corrects react-pdf (a viewer) versus @react-pdf/renderer (a\n  generator), which were conflated in the categories overview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbef545ce2eedd13f4c901626822e6b46004ed2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/bbef545ce2eedd13f4c901626822e6b46004ed2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDAxY2NmMTczZjVlZDMzMGE5ZTY1ZjVjZTc5NGFiNDBhNTBhOGJiNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b","sha":"73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b"}],"sha":"01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/01ccf173f5ed330a9e65f5ce794ab40a50a8bb69"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:23:08Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:23:08Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add reading-progress marks to engineering failures reference\n\nAlso regenerates the table of contents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4b2ce8a3ab6ec39407b726242d612d7112f5981","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/d4b2ce8a3ab6ec39407b726242d612d7112f5981"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDczYTYzMmVjY2Y0Y2Q0OWRkMzEzMjVjNDAwZWQyOThkNmQ5ZTdlMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95","sha":"94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95"}],"sha":"73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/73a632eccf4cd49dd31325c400ed298d6d9e7e2b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:23:08Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T21:23:08Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add Prettier config pinning 2-space indentation\n\nThe editor''s global prettier.tabWidth was 4, which reformatted generated\nfiles on save. A project config keeps this repo at 2 spaces regardless of\nmachine. Mirrors the other Prettier settings that were previously coming\nfrom editor config, since a config file overrides those entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"025ea86b5abe51a1e2237ebd72d5495d2031db21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/025ea86b5abe51a1e2237ebd72d5495d2031db21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDk0ODE3ZDdlNmMwMWZiNmNmZDY0YjQzMjljMzI1MjgxYTE3YzJhOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3","sha":"a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3"}],"sha":"94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/94817d7e6c01fb6cfd64b4329c325281a17c2a95"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T22:33:31Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T22:33:31Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add staff-plus engineering judgement references\n\nSix cross-linked files covering the senior to staff to principal gap,\nwhich the existing material only touched in passing:\n\n- ENGINEERING-FAILURES: famous outages and their real causes, the\n  architectural decisions that sink projects, organisational failure\n  modes, and the blameless post-mortem\n- TECHNICAL-DECISION-MAKING: reversibility, build vs buy, boring\n  technology, rewrite vs refactor, ADRs and RFCs, making the case to\n  non-engineers, and decision anti-patterns\n- STAFF-PLUS-ENGINEER: what changes above senior, the four archetypes,\n  influence without authority, sponsorship, glue work, promotion\n- LEGACY-MIGRATION: strangler fig, branch by abstraction,\n  expand-contract schema changes, zero-downtime data migration,\n  monolith decomposition, and the organisational half\n- INCIDENT-RESPONSE: severity, incident command, mitigate before\n  diagnose, communication, runbooks, SLOs and error budgets, on-call\n- TECHNICAL-DEBT: the four quadrants, hotspot analysis, the business\n  case, repayment strategies, and when not to pay\n\nAlso corrects the file counts in README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ceb80432ed0a55bd78b7fa1e4f20cac7bb36d27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/6ceb80432ed0a55bd78b7fa1e4f20cac7bb36d27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKGE5NDkxMDcyZjIwNTYzYjIwNDYyY2NiZDQ5OGYzYzYwNTQ2NWZjYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6","sha":"5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6"}],"sha":"a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/a9491072f20563b20462ccbd498f3c605465fcc3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:48:42Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:48:42Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add non-functional requirements beginner guide\n\nCovers the functional versus non-functional distinction, why quality\nattributes are what actually sink projects, and one section per\ncategory: performance and percentiles, scalability, availability and\nreliability with RPO/RTO, security, maintainability, usability and\naccessibility, observability, compatibility, compliance and cost.\n\nAlso how to write a measurable NFR, the trade-offs between them, where\nrequirements come from, how to verify each type, how to use them in a\nsystem design interview, a reusable checklist, and common mistakes.\n\nPreviously only passing mentions across a few files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"699250aac587d1584755627dd45075715cb723e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/699250aac587d1584755627dd45075715cb723e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDVjNTA3ZDIzZWMzMTQ1NmUxNTIzZDY2YjE2ZjFkMDNiOGNjMzQ0ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb","sha":"e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb"}],"sha":"5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/5c507d23ec31456e1523d66b16f1d03b8cc344d6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:34:18Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:34:18Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Reorganise Tailwind reference and add transform vs transition\n\nRewrites the section 14 class reference from two interleaved columns to\na single column grouped by feature, and fills in the gaps the cramped\nlayout had squeezed out: grid, positioning, group-hover and dark\nprefixes, breakpoint pixel values, and how the colour shade scale works.\n\nAdds a subsection to section 13 explaining transform (what the change\nis) versus transition (how it happens), with the delete-each-one test.\n\nAlso includes reading-progress marks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"942f5c4d86447c0e9f64a03c454f1fb974ab8c2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/942f5c4d86447c0e9f64a03c454f1fb974ab8c2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKGU5YWNkMDZlYzBlN2Y0NWIzYTMzODM3ZmVmYTc5Y2FkY2U5MTNjZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750","sha":"2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750"}],"sha":"e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/e9acd06ec0e7f45b3a33837fefa79cadce913ceb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:44:41Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:44:41Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add Vitest vs Jest comparison to testing guide\n\nCovers the near-identical API, the underlying engine difference (Vite\nand esbuild versus Babel transforms), the two gotchas when moving a\nJest test across, and which to pick.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1cdd8e3558d91e8b493fdf41ada93b2fbfb288d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/f1cdd8e3558d91e8b493fdf41ada93b2fbfb288d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDJmZDdmM2IyNjVmYWI1YzY1ZGJmZDYyZjBmNTA2NzgwMmJlOTU3NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99","sha":"bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99"}],"sha":"2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/2fd7f3b265fab5c65dbfd62f0f5067802be95750"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:32:12Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:32:12Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Expand DI and test-double explanations in testing guide\n\nAdds a plain-words explanation of why constructor injection makes a\nservice testable, and a much simpler treatment of stub/mock/spy/fake:\nan analogy, the same four in one running code example, and a short\ndecision guide.\n\nAlso includes reading-progress marks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5085dec81cb75ed6c3e60386424a9d404095be5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/b5085dec81cb75ed6c3e60386424a9d404095be5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKGJmZGVmZDFjMDJjZTlhYWQyYjliNDc1YWI0NjRhYWEyZDE1MDRiOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e","sha":"9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e"}],"sha":"bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/bfdefd1c02ce9aad2b9b475ab464aaa2d1504b99"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:04:29Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:04:29Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add PDF rendering and generation reference\n\nCovers the file format internals (objects, xref, content stream\noperators, compression), how PDF.js renders in the browser including\nthe invisible text layer, the three backend generation strategies and\nwhen each applies, headless Chrome and PDFKit in practice, where PDF\nwork belongs in an architecture, manipulation and extraction, fonts,\nsecurity, performance, and a library decision table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"693c1c989d485ccf35e6e1ac3ae433c8e1b8b46a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/693c1c989d485ccf35e6e1ac3ae433c8e1b8b46a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/commits/9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e","node_id":"C_kwDOSbboJNoAKDljNjZjODQ3MWE3MDU1N2YyMGU0YjhhNWVjY2Y4Y2I1ZGFkOWM0NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commit/cf580858105f32d2f45fd8b25396f6bc52d07d3f","sha":"cf580858105f32d2f45fd8b25396f6bc52d07d3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/cf580858105f32d2f45fd8b25396f6bc52d07d3f"}],"sha":"9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/9c66c8471a70557f20e4b8a5eccf8cb5dad9c46e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/commits/cf580858105f32d2f45fd8b25396f6bc52d07d3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:04:29Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T22:04:29Z","email":"hairui@gophr.app","name":"HairuiWang96"},"message":"Add reading-progress marks to CSS and testing guides\n\nAlso regenerates tables of contents and reformats code blocks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a0ade7660881ba0e7a610b4be84e88bd2242156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HairuiWang96/taskboard/git/trees/4a0ade7660881ba0e7a610b4be84e88bd2242156"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/