ub.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/ab72c3f076c1b9424a52a85499d3421aa5e21779/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T19:06:16Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T19:06:16Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Rebuild clinic SPA: hide redundant LID JID line on WhatsApp page\n\nSibling of prime-mate-clinic commit 7442721. Cleans up the chat\nheader so it shows the number only — no ''@s.whatsapp.net'' or\n''@lid'' clutter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"844a0d56a55a746a3222efbcd122881fc337a2a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/844a0d56a55a746a3222efbcd122881fc337a2a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/ab72c3f076c1b9424a52a85499d3421aa5e21779","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/ab72c3f076c1b9424a52a85499d3421aa5e21779","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGFiNzJjM2YwNzZjMWI5NDI0YTUyYTg1NDk5ZDM0MjFhYTVlMjE3Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54","sha":"afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54"}],"sha":"ab72c3f076c1b9424a52a85499d3421aa5e21779","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/ab72c3f076c1b9424a52a85499d3421aa5e21779"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T19:03:03Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T19:03:03Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp: handle LID (privacy ID) chats end-to-end\n\nWhatsApp privacy IDs (LIDs) are how Business accounts / privacy-\nmode contacts identify themselves WITHOUT exposing a phone\nnumber. Wasender returns these as \"233908264300569@lid\" with NO\nLID-to-phone mapping in /contacts on this plan tier (verified\nvia the new /raw_contacts diagnostic). So we treat LID chats as\nfirst-class but read-only.\n\nNew module backend/app/demos/clinic/whatsapp_contacts.py:\n- In-memory cache of Wasender''s /contacts (10-min TTL).\n- is_lid_jid / is_phone_jid / is_group_jid classifiers.\n- async lookup(jid) + display_name_for(jid) (picks notify /\n  verifiedName / name in that order).\n- Never raises — silent failures preserve the existing cache.\n\n/whatsapp/chats endpoint now returns per chat:\n- display_name (push name from contacts) — friendlier than the\n  raw 15-digit LID.\n- is_lid bool — flag for the SPA to gate reply / patient-link.\n\n/whatsapp/send refuses LID targets up front with a clear error\n(\"Cannot send to a WhatsApp LID (privacy ID). The sender hasn''t\nexposed their phone number...\"). Defence-in-depth on top of the\nSPA''s disabled reply button.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle (sibling commit on\nprime-mate-clinic disables the reply form, badges LID chats, and\nskips patient lookup for them).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5354af4bda1a613e57982e32a9a707d594e9a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/a5354af4bda1a613e57982e32a9a707d594e9a82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGFmZDYzNTA4NWEzNTZjMDgxYmQ0ZjgzODkxODkwYzM3NGJjZDljNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4","sha":"82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4"}],"sha":"afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/afd635085a356c081bd4f83891890c374bcd9c54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:53:28Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:53:28Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp: add /raw_contacts diagnostic endpoint\n\nDumps Wasender''s raw /contacts response so we can see whether\neach contact carries both a phone and a LID — needed to resolve\nincoming WhatsApp LIDs (e.g. 233908264300569@lid) back to real\nphone numbers on the chat list and patient-linking flow.\n\nBackend-only, no SPA rebuild needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af14ea0331fd7dd1ebf280d8df61ab812c460fae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/af14ea0331fd7dd1ebf280d8df61ab812c460fae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDgyZjA5MjBiYTE0YzA3M2QxZmYzYjIzY2FiZjMwOGJjMGZlNTIxYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f","sha":"911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f"}],"sha":"82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/82f0920ba14c073d1ff3b23cabf308bc0fe521c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:51:52Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:51:52Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp /raw: bump cap to 500 + echo Wasender pagination wrapper\n\nOperator hitting /whatsapp/raw?limit=20 was getting only 10 rows\nbecause Wasender''s Laravel paginator caps message-logs at\n~10/page. Couldn''t see the inbound LID row that the /chats\nendpoint had clearly found (different request, different limit).\n\n- Bump our internal cap from min(20) to min(500). Wasender''s\n  client wrapper already validates against its own max.\n- Surface Wasender''s pagination wrapper (data, current_page,\n  last_page, total, next_page_url, etc.) via the new\n  raw_wrapper field so the operator can see whether there''s\n  more data behind a higher page= request.\n\nBackend-only, no SPA rebuild needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f19747046f6f25d37a7a4430542ba686156c3ffb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/f19747046f6f25d37a7a4430542ba686156c3ffb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDkxMWM3NmQxODAxMTgzNzhhMGEzYTQyZDhkYmIwMmI1Yjc3ZWZmOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a","sha":"f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a"}],"sha":"911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/911c76d180118378a0a3a42d8dbb02b5b77eff9f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:21:18Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:21:18Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: include clinic name in list_patient_appointments rows\n\nUser reported: \"agent pulled the correct timing but the wrong\nclinic\" when reading back an appointment. Root cause was that\n_appt_for_agent only returned clinic_id (\"DEP-003\"), not the\nclinic''s name. The agent then had to cross-reference the\nsystem-instruction''s roster block to figure out the human-readable\nname — drifting to the wrong one occasionally.\n\n_appt_for_agent now accepts a clinics_by_id lookup table and\nadds clinic_name / clinic_name_ar / clinic_location /\nclinic_location_ar inline on each appointment row.\n_t_list_patient_appointments builds the lookup table once per\ncall and threads it through.\n\nSubsequent reschedule / cancel paths already had the clinic\nrecord in hand from their own snapshot reads, so no other call\nsites needed the new signature — the default (clinics_by_id=None)\nkeeps backwards compatibility if someone calls _appt_for_agent\nwithout it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ccb39d7c4e7d57432149f0a623737c3e479f99a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/9ccb39d7c4e7d57432149f0a623737c3e479f99a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGYyZmQyNjFlNmY0ZGY4ZWJlNTRhZWM4YmQ1MmY1MDRiZmZjNjNjNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd","sha":"ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd"}],"sha":"f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/f2fd261e6f4df8ebe54aec8bd52f504bffc63c4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:06:20Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T18:06:20Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: summarise slot ranges instead of reciting each one\n\nUX fix from the office. When list_free_slots returns a six-slot\nafternoon block like 14:00 → 16:30, the agent was saying\n\"2:00 and 2:30 and 3:00 and 3:30 and 4:00 and 4:30\" — every\nslot, six \"and\"s. Caller-hostile.\n\nNew _GUARDRAILS block \"Summarise contiguous slot ranges — never\nrecite every 30 minutes\" tells the agent to speak the range\n(\"anything from 2:00 PM through 4:30 PM, every half hour\")\nwhen slots are contiguous, segment them on gaps, and only read\nindividually for 1-3 slot edge cases. Bilingual examples for\nboth EN and AR.\n\nSPA persona seed mirrors. Includes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"159fe9d8000e9c05c5ede58403864b460c888a46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/159fe9d8000e9c05c5ede58403864b460c888a46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGViYzlhZTk5OGVhMDRmMDk2NzczYTg5ODNkMzdjZWFmZDJlMmI5Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373","sha":"8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373"}],"sha":"ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/ebc9ae998ea04f096773a8983d37ceafd2e2b9cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T14:01:20Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T14:01:20Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: surface AMI dial_supervisor failures in the Debug page\n\nUser reported \"Listen/Whisper/Barge button doesn''t call the\nextension\" with no obvious error. Two fixes:\n\n1. dial_supervisor now logs an ENTRY line at INFO showing the\n   non-secret credentials it loaded (host, port, username,\n   secret-set flag) and the target extension + spy_mode. The\n   early-exit returns (\"AMI credentials incomplete\",\n   \"supervisor_extension not configured\") now also log at\n   WARNING with the human-readable error. Previously a missing\n   config silently returned a JSON error and the Debug page\n   showed nothing.\n\n2. demo_clinic.ami logger is now in the _install_debug_handler\n   target list, so all AMI traffic (connect failures, login\n   rejection, channel discovery diag, originate response) flows\n   to the Call Center → Debug page in real time. Previously\n   only console output showed those.\n\n3. The error messages themselves now explicitly remind the\n   operator that escalation.json is per-machine (gitignored),\n   so values from the other machine don''t sync — the most\n   common cause of \"it worked yesterday\" failures after a\n   fresh git pull on a new box.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle (Dashboard failure-state\ncolouring sibling commit on prime-mate-clinic).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c8e1f554bea38d1f8b02a6c34d30c1906eedda8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/8c8e1f554bea38d1f8b02a6c34d30c1906eedda8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDhiNTA1NjZkOTcxMmY4ZGI1OWU1NjhiMTA0OTQ5ODkzMWM0MTQzNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84","sha":"6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84"}],"sha":"8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8b50566d9712f8db59e568b1049498931c414373"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T13:47:40Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T13:47:40Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: log tool results + persona rules vs two real bugs\n\nReal-call regression captured by the new Debug page logs:\n\n  16:30:48.827  dispatch list_free_slots\n  16:30:48.834  dispatch create_appointment time=13:30   ← 7 ms later\n  16:30:49.811  fabrication detected: slot_time ''01:30''\n\nThe agent fired list_free_slots and create_appointment in the\nSAME Gemini turn (parallel function calls). It didn''t wait for\nthe slot list — booked a guessed time that landed in the\nclinic''s break window. Then retried with 14:00 once the rejection\ncame back. From the caller''s POV the agent offered a slot that\ndidn''t exist.\n\nSeparate issue: agent hung up right after create_patient. The\nnew \"whatsapp_sent\": true field on mutation responses (added so\nthe agent doesn''t double-send) was being read as \"everything''s\ndone, end the call\".\n\nThree fixes:\n\n1. execute_tool now logs RESULTS too, not just dispatches.\n   - On error: WARNING with the error message.\n   - On success: INFO with a curated summary (ok, patient_id,\n     file_number, appointment_id, date, time, *_count for list\n     responses, whatsapp_sent, etc.) — never the full payload\n     so the Debug page stays readable.\n   - Refactored execute_tool into a thin wrapper around\n     _execute_tool_inner so before/after logging happens once,\n     not at every branch return.\n\n2. New _GUARDRAILS block \"NEVER call list_free_slots and\n   create_appointment in the SAME turn\" — explicitly forbids\n   parallel function calls for booking. Spells out the strict\n   two-turn flow (list → wait → read to caller → create) and\n   tells the agent the bug it would cause if it ignored.\n\n3. New _GUARDRAILS block \"End_call discipline — auto-WhatsApp\n   does NOT mean ''done''\" — clarifies that whatsapp_sent: true\n   on a tool response means \"I sent it so you don''t have to\",\n   NOT \"the call is over\". Wait for explicit caller goodbye.\n\nSPA persona seed mirrors both new blocks. Includes the rebuilt\nclinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a49a723d0c12c382ceed961fcb4d1328259a4da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/1a49a723d0c12c382ceed961fcb4d1328259a4da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDZiNDAyYTMwOWU2NjlmMTI3MjdiNjExNTQ4NmY1OWY0ZmFlMGZjODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c","sha":"a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c"}],"sha":"6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/6b402a309e669f12727b6115486f59f4fae0fc84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T13:22:49Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T13:22:49Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: real-time debug stream + ctx hygiene at create_patient\n\nTwo related changes:\n\n1. New debug-log fan-out: every LogRecord emitted by the clinic\n   modules (live_agent, agent_tools, wasender, whatsapp_inbox,\n   whatsapp_templates) is now broadcast to /agent/ws as a `debug`\n   event the moment it''s logged. The SPA''s new Call Center →\n   Debug page renders the stream in real time, with filters by\n   level/logger/text and Pause / Clear controls.\n\n   Implementation: _DebugBroadcastHandler at the bottom of\n   live_agent.py, installed at module import via\n   _install_debug_handler() on every relevant logger.\n   Idempotent — survives uvicorn --reload without duplicating\n   handlers.\n\n   Extra debug instrumentation at known weak spots:\n   - execute_tool() now emits a compact \"dispatch <name>\n     args=… call_id=… ids=…\" line so the Debug page shows\n     every tool the agent invokes with which arguments.\n   - _auto_send_template() logs the to/lang on entry, then\n     either \"OK (message_id=…)\" or \"FAILED: <error>\" on exit.\n   - _t_create_patient() now logs the SAVED record (id, file,\n     name, phone).\n\n2. ctx hygiene at create_patient — fixes the related \"agent\n   creates patient then immediately tries list_free_slots and\n   gets blocked by the no-patient-context nudge\" failure:\n\n   - The newly-created patient_id is now added to\n     ctx[''identified_patient_ids''] (which lives on the\n     CallSession), so subsequent scheduling tools recognise the\n     caller as identified without needing a separate lookup.\n   - ctx[''caller_phone''] is stamped from the create_patient''s\n     phone arg when previously empty, so the auto-send template\n     finds the number even when the agent never ran a\n     lookup_patient_by_phone first.\n\n   Without this fix, the demoer''s test pattern (call → minimal\n   intake → book) would frequently fail because the create_patient\n   succeeded but the new patient wasn''t yet in the identified set.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle with the Debug page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"35a478e1e1cbcd49319dd2a55abcdef3596e7612","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/35a478e1e1cbcd49319dd2a55abcdef3596e7612"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGExNjZmMTA2YjUyMjkwOTM0NzBiZThjZGQwNTI2Y2ViOTkxMzAyMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5","sha":"d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5"}],"sha":"a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/a166f106b5229093470be8cdd0526ceb9913021c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:38:53Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:38:53Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: auto-send WhatsApp templates from mutation tools\n\nMove the four event-driven WhatsApp templates from \"the agent\nmust remember to call send_whatsapp_template\" to \"the runtime\nfires them automatically on every successful mutation\". The\nagent kept forgetting; now it doesn''t have to remember.\n\nSide-effect map:\n  _t_create_patient        → file_creation\n  _t_create_appointment    → appointment_creation\n  _t_cancel_appointment    → appointment_cancellation\n  _t_reschedule_appointment → appointment_reschedule\n\nEach mutation tool calls a new _auto_send_template(template_id,\nctx, variables) helper after save_snapshot() succeeds. The\nhelper:\n  - reuses the existing _t_send_whatsapp_template path\n    (rendering, phone normalisation, Wasender send, tool_mutation\n    broadcast), so the Dashboard activity feed and message id\n    flow unchanged;\n  - swallows errors (logs at INFO) so a WhatsApp failure can''t\n    roll back the underlying record write;\n  - defaults language to ''ar'' (matches the persona''s Arabic-\n    first stance) — operator can override later by editing the\n    template body or, when ctx[''call_language''] is wired, by\n    the agent passing language.\n\nEach tool''s response now carries \"whatsapp_sent\": true so the\nagent knows the send happened — the persona''s GUARDRAILS block\n\"WhatsApp templates — runtime auto-sends them; you DON''T need\nto\" tells the agent NOT to also call send_whatsapp_template for\nthe four mutations (would double-send). The only template the\nagent fires by hand is clinic_location, which is a non-mutation\n\"caller asked for the address\" moment.\n\nFor create_patient, we have no specific clinic in scope at\nintake time, so we pick the first active clinic from the\nsnapshot as a sensible default for {clinic_name} /\n{clinic_name_ar} placeholders. The operator can edit the\nfile_creation template to remove the clinic line if they prefer\na fully generic body.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3cd9862ec02e3287cde1a9f60f10a18bcb455e28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/3cd9862ec02e3287cde1a9f60f10a18bcb455e28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGQwMTBiZGQ2OGVjYWY1N2JmODAzZDNjMjk3NzI4ZDQxYmRiMjI1ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c","sha":"3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c"}],"sha":"d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d010bdd68ecaf57bf803d3c297728d41bdb225f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:11:50Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T12:11:50Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: minimal intake — name + phone only\n\nStop collecting national ID, date of birth, city, and reason for\nvisit over the phone. Those are now captured at the front desk\non arrival. Persona collects ONLY name + mobile, then creates\nthe file and tells the caller the rest is at reception.\n\nThree persona blocks updated to keep this consistent:\n\n- DEFAULT_PERSONA \"Caller intake flow\" — returning patients can\n  identify by file # OR phone (no ID + DOB cross-confirm);\n  new patients only get asked for name + mobile.\n- _GUARDRAILS \"Intake — minimal. Name and phone. That''s it.\"\n  replaces the previous six-field intake. Spells out the 9-step\n  flow: ask name → confirm → ask phone → confirm digit-by-digit\n  → call create_patient with only those two → read back\n  file_number → tell caller \"rest at reception\" → fire\n  WhatsApp file_creation template → move on. Hard rules: don''t\n  reintroduce ID/DOB/city even if the caller volunteers them\n  (reception captures), and don''t ask for reason for visit\n  during intake.\n- DEFAULT_PERSONA \"Booking flow\" no longer re-asks for name +\n  phone since intake already covered them. Trims to: clinic /\n  specialty → date + time from list_free_slots → confirm →\n  create_appointment → fire appointment_creation template.\n\nThe create_patient tool already accepts name as the only\nrequired field (with all the others optional), so no tool\nchanges are needed — this is purely a persona simplification.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d21cad7a75093cae5d1ddeb299ec59b0db8de61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/7d21cad7a75093cae5d1ddeb299ec59b0db8de61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDM5MTRhZmU5YTg3ZjNmNDdlZDAxZTQ1N2Y2M2ZiMmQ4ZDRiNWFkMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe","sha":"bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe"}],"sha":"3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/3914afe9a87f3f47ed01e457f63fb2d8d4b5ad1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T11:28:44Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T11:28:44Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: appointment ownership enforcement + gender guardrail\n\nThree issues from a real call, two of them safety-critical:\n\n1. (SAFETY) Agent cancelled an appointment belonging to a\n   different patient after caller identification. The persona\n   said don''t; the model did anyway. Backend now ENFORCES it:\n\n   - CallSession''s identified_patient_ids set is now exposed\n     through tool_ctx and kept in sync (lookups + create_patient\n     both populate it; mutated in-place so all subsequent tool\n     calls see the latest membership).\n   - cancel_appointment, reschedule_appointment, and\n     list_patient_appointments now refuse with an explicit error\n     if the appointment''s patient_id isn''t in the identified set\n     (or if NOBODY is identified yet — deny by default rather\n     than allow, so an anonymous caller can''t fish for IDs).\n   - The refusal message tells the agent exactly which flow to\n     follow next: lookup → list_patient_appointments → act on\n     ids from THAT list.\n\n2. send_whatsapp_template failed with \"No phone to send to —\n   caller_phone unknown\" even after the caller was identified.\n   Tool now falls back: explicit to_phone → ctx.caller_phone →\n   any identified patient''s phone in the snapshot. Plus\n   tool_ctx[''caller_phone''] is now mirrored from the receive\n   loop whenever a lookup populates session.caller_phone, so\n   the next tool call sees the latest value.\n\n3. Agent used feminine Arabic forms with a male caller. New\n   _GUARDRAILS block \"Arabic gender — DEFAULT MASCULINE, switch\n   ONLY on hard evidence\" lists the three (and only three)\n   triggers that justify switching, and clarifies that Layla''s\n   own voice gender is unrelated to the caller''s gender.\n\nPlus a new _GUARDRAILS block \"NEVER touch another caller''s\nappointment\" that mirrors the runtime enforcement above and\nexplicitly bans the same-household exception (\"my wife''s\nappointment\").\n\nSPA persona seed mirrors both new blocks. Includes the rebuilt\nclinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d673d38b7109e91b795996f2d087742d7b62eef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/1d673d38b7109e91b795996f2d087742d7b62eef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGJmOTVlZDNiMzA0OTk1OTQ1NGZjYzkyNzFhOTdhNmVmYjJhNmVkYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c","sha":"fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c"}],"sha":"bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/bf95ed3b3049959454fcc9271a97a6efb2a6edbe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T09:15:42Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T09:15:42Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp templates: agent tool + 5 default templates + editor backend\n\nThe Live Agent can now fire pre-canned WhatsApp templates during\na call (booking confirmations, file numbers, clinic location).\nFive templates ship with English + Arabic bodies; the operator\nedits them on the new SPA page (Call Center → WhatsApp\nTemplates), the file is checked into git so both machines stay\nin sync, and the agent picks the language matching the call.\n\nBackend pieces:\n\n- backend/app/demos/clinic/whatsapp_templates.py — module with\n  the five DEFAULT_TEMPLATES (clinic_location, file_creation,\n  appointment_creation, appointment_reschedule,\n  appointment_cancellation), each carrying name/description/\n  variables/en/ar. resolved_templates() merges defaults +\n  on-disk overrides; render() interpolates {placeholders} with\n  empty-string fallback for missing keys.\n\n- agent_tools.py — new send_whatsapp_template tool declared\n  with one required field (template_id, language) plus every\n  variable as an optional string. Dispatcher routes to\n  _t_send_whatsapp_template which renders, normalises the\n  phone via wasender.normalize_phone, sends via the per-session\n  API key (sync httpx.Client so the existing sync execute_tool\n  doesn''t need refactoring), and broadcasts a tool_mutation\n  event of kind whatsapp_template_sent for the Dashboard''s\n  activity feed.\n\n- router.py — GET/POST /api/demo/clinic/whatsapp/templates,\n  partial-merge updates only the locales that changed.\n\n- live_agent.py _GUARDRAILS — documents send_whatsapp_template\n  with the \"fire IMMEDIATELY after the matching tool\" rule for\n  each of the five templates.\n\n.gitignore: whatsapp_templates.json now travels through git\n(content, not state), matching the persona.txt / kb.txt\ncarve-out. Added matching entry for whatsapp_inbox.json\n(which had been added in §6e but never explicitly listed).\nCLAUDE.md updated to mention the third tracked file.\n\nBundle: includes the SPA page + sidebar entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d93771665e3107ef38cce56e7d13a47ee611c52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/9d93771665e3107ef38cce56e7d13a47ee611c52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGZiZTZiOWUyNmFjYjVhODI3ZWQ1ZjJjMzZjMGFlZjcwYTRlM2RmMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b","sha":"c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b"}],"sha":"fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/fbe6b9e26acb5a827ed5f2c36c0aef70a4e3df1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:56:12Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:56:12Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp inbox: receive via webhook + merge with outbound logs\n\nWasenderApi''s /whatsapp-sessions/{id}/message-logs is outbound-\nonly, so the operator could send messages but never see replies.\nAdd the missing inbound half:\n\n- New module backend/app/demos/clinic/whatsapp_inbox.py — file-\n  backed ring buffer at data/demos/clinic/whatsapp_inbox.json\n  (gitignored, capped at 2000 rows). Thread-safe (webhook + UI\n  request can race), atomic file replace, dedupe on message id.\n\n- POST /api/demo/clinic/whatsapp/webhook accepts any JSON shape\n  Wasender posts, deep-walks for message-row dicts (so we don''t\n  care which envelope variant a given Wasender tier uses), and\n  persists them with a server-stamped received_at + source tag.\n  Returns {ok, added} so the operator can sanity-check from a\n  curl that rows are being stored.\n\n- GET /api/demo/clinic/whatsapp/inbox?limit=50 reads the store\n  back (mostly for diagnostics).\n- DELETE /api/demo/clinic/whatsapp/inbox wipes it.\n\n- /whatsapp/chats and /whatsapp/messages now concatenate\n  outbound_logs + list_inbox() before grouping / filtering. The\n  same direction-detection heuristics handle both sides; the\n  new received_at field is picked up by _msg_ts.\n\n- /whatsapp/status surface now includes inbox_stored + inbox_last_ts\n  so the SPA can flag if no webhook has ever landed.\n\nWiring on the operator side (one-time per machine):\n  1. Expose the backend publicly (ngrok / cloudflared tunnel\n     works for demos).\n  2. WasenderApi dashboard → Webhooks → Add webhook → URL is\n     <public-host>/api/demo/clinic/whatsapp/webhook → tick\n     \"Message Received\" events.\n  3. Send a test message; watch the backend log for\n     \"WhatsApp webhook stored N new message(s)\".\n\nBundle: includes the SPA patient-linking change from the sibling\ncommit on prime-mate-clinic. Plus DEMOSITEMAP §6e documenting\nthe webhook setup + patient-linking flow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b7986ee7bc4044a256b9343bd45748bdfdd112c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/4b7986ee7bc4044a256b9343bd45748bdfdd112c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGMyNDQ1YmM5NjliNmExYThmNDEzMjBkOTQyZTRlZWMzZWEyNWQzOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067","sha":"4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067"}],"sha":"c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c2445bc969b6a1a8f41320d942e4eec3ea25d39b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:31:22Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:31:22Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp inbox: auto-detect direction via our paired number\n\nEvery message rendered on the left side (caller alignment) because\n_msg_from_me always returned false — none of our explicit fields\n(fromMe, direction, isOutgoing, …) matched WasenderApi''s actual\nmessage-logs shape.\n\nAdd a self-bootstrapping detector: across the whole batch of rows,\nthe phone number that appears in the most messages is our paired\nWhatsApp number (it''s in every conversation; partner numbers each\nappear only in one). _detect_our_phone() finds it, and the new\n_msg_from_me(m, our_digits) compares m.from / m.sender against\nthat number — if they match, the message is outgoing.\n\nThe detector kicks in as the LAST heuristic, so explicit signals\nstill win when they exist. Both /whatsapp/chats and\n/whatsapp/messages call _detect_our_phone once per request and\nthread the digits through. The detected number is also exposed in\nthe response as `our_digits` so the SPA can use it later for\nsender labels if needed.\n\nAlso picked up a few more direction-marker keys (sentByMe,\nmessageDirection, flow, is_sent_by_me) and started accepting\nstatus in {sent, delivered, read, playing, played, pending} as a\nstrong outbound signal — only outbound rows ever reach those\nstatuses in WhatsApp''s protocol.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"80c21ba8996f440a350601e42d4b412c2d4246b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/80c21ba8996f440a350601e42d4b412c2d4246b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDQ5NTBkODczZGNjMzQxZDYxMWFkZjFmMGRlYjBkNTZhMzUxNGQwNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3","sha":"c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3"}],"sha":"4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/4950d873dcc341d611adf1f0deb0d56a3514d067"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:22:55Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:22:55Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp inbox: handle Wasender''s message-body field + JID variants\n\nTwo symptoms from the same root cause: every message in the inbox\nrendered as the literal placeholder \"[text]\" (and freshly-arrived\nreplies appeared to never show up — because they looked identical\nto all the older messages already rendered as [text]).\n\nCause: _msg_text only knew Baileys-style envelopes\n(message.conversation, message.extendedTextMessage.text, etc.) plus\na short list of flat top-level keys. WasenderApi''s message-logs\nresponse uses fields we hadn''t enumerated, so the extractor fell\nall the way through to the \"messageType: text\" placeholder.\n\nFix is in three layers:\n\n1. _msg_text now tries a much wider set of explicit paths\n   (messageText, messageContent, message_body, text_body, msg,\n   caption, etc., each tried both flat and nested one level\n   deeper) and then falls back to a recursive deep scan that\n   returns the LONGEST plausible string in the row, skipping a\n   blocklist of obvious non-body keys (ids, timestamps, JIDs,\n   status, direction, …) and any string that contains\n   @s.whatsapp.net / @g.us. Real bodies are almost always the\n   longest free-text field in a row, so this catches Wasender''s\n   shape regardless of the exact key name.\n\n2. _msg_jid widened to the same set of candidates (sender,\n   recipient, phone, number, chat_id, key.remoteJid) plus a\n   recursive fallback that returns the first @s.whatsapp.net /\n   @g.us string it finds. Bare-digit values get normalised to\n   \"<digits>@s.whatsapp.net\" so grouping stays consistent.\n\n3. /whatsapp/messages now matches the selected jid against the\n   message rows on a DIGITS-ONLY comparison (in addition to the\n   exact-string equality). A row might store the chat key as\n   \"9665…@s.whatsapp.net\", \"9665…\", or \"+9665…\" depending on the\n   endpoint variant — comparing on digits sidesteps that.\n\nPlus _msg_from_me picked up a few more direction markers\n(is_outgoing, isOutgoing, outgoing, \"send\"/\"receive\").\n\nNew endpoint GET /api/demo/clinic/whatsapp/raw?limit=5 dumps the\nfirst N message-log rows verbatim, bypassing our normalisation.\nUseful diagnostic when a Wasender plan tier returns a shape we\nhaven''t seen — the user can hit it and paste the result so we know\nexactly which key to add to the explicit list.\n\nBackend-only, no SPA rebuild needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11879b1f60d92b094725621f4d5a2a60842c5ab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/11879b1f60d92b094725621f4d5a2a60842c5ab1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGM5NGExZTRhZTdiYTk5ZWRkMzViNzJjOGQ2NTI4ZTBiNzliNWViYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2","sha":"8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2"}],"sha":"c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c94a1e4ae7ba99edd35b72c8d6528e0b79b5ebc3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:13:50Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:13:50Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"WhatsApp: Personal Access Token support + per-endpoint token picker\n\nWasenderApi splits auth between two scopes:\n  - per-session API key: POST /send-message, GET /contacts\n  - account-level Personal Access Token (PAT):\n    everything under /whatsapp-sessions/{id}/* (message logs,\n    session metadata)\n\nThe previous client only stored the session API key and used it\nfor all endpoints, so the inbox view failed with:\n  \"This endpoint requires a valid personal access token.\"\nThe Configuration page had no field for the PAT either.\n\nBackend:\n  - escalation.json now stores wasender_personal_token alongside\n    wasender_api_key and wasender_session_id.\n  - WasenderCredentials carries both; new can_send / can_read_inbox\n    helpers replace the old is_complete.\n  - _headers(prefer=\"api_key\"|\"personal\") picks the right token\n    per endpoint with the other as a fallback (some Wasender plans\n    accept the session key for /whatsapp-sessions/* — we don''t\n    want to lock those out).\n  - send_text → prefer=\"api_key\"; ping → prefer=\"api_key\";\n    list_messages → prefer=\"personal\".\n  - All router callers pass both tokens through build_wasender_client.\n  - GET /whatsapp/status now reports personal_token_configured so\n    the SPA can show a useful hint instead of just the raw\n    upstream error.\n\nBundle: includes the SPA changes (compose dialog + PAT field).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9dd9411a4acaccf69ac217f7eb7ba5054f7a282","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/f9dd9411a4acaccf69ac217f7eb7ba5054f7a282"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDg2Mzg5NTAwNzYzMDJjN2Q0MzI2OGYwNTkyNDA0YjY1OGM2MmQ5ZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a","sha":"0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a"}],"sha":"8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8638950076302c7d43268f0592404b658c62d9e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:01:38Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T08:01:38Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Track persona.txt / kb.txt across machines via git\n\nThe Live Agent reads persona.txt and kb.txt off disk on every call\nso the SPA''s \"Apply to Live Agent\" button persists across restarts.\nThose files were being swept into the broad `data/demos/` ignore,\nwhich meant clicking Apply on one machine left the other machine\non a stale (or default) persona — same demo, different agent\nbehaviour depending on which machine answered the phone.\n\nNarrow the ignore: instead of excluding the whole `data/demos/`\ntree, exclude only the per-machine bits — `calls/` (caller PII),\n`snapshot.json` (patient PII), `escalation.json` (AMI password +\nWasender API key) — and let everything else through. Persona and\nKB now travel through git like any other content.\n\nCommit the current persona.txt as the canonical version going\nforward. Future \"Apply to Live Agent\" clicks should be committed +\npushed so both machines stay in sync; CLAUDE.md updated to\ndocument the carve-out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3eaf1c60a5ff2cc1862081dcae78bdf3d7290250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/3eaf1c60a5ff2cc1862081dcae78bdf3d7290250"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDBjMTJjM2Y3ODczMWVlZWUwZDRjYmQ5MzAzMTQ2ZTA5MDE4OWU1OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90","sha":"23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90"}],"sha":"0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/0c12c3f78731eeee0d4cbd9303146e090189e58a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T07:57:06Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T07:57:06Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: structural nudge when scheduling without patient_id\n\nUser reported: agent collected and confirmed intake details, but\nnever called create_patient — so the file was never saved, and\nthe agent then jumped to list_free_slots which produced past-day\nslot offers (\"9:00\", \"10:30\" at a 10:53 AM call) that the\nfabrication detector correctly flagged.\n\nThe flag was right but the underlying failure (no create_patient)\nwas the cause. Closes both with a single structural fix:\n\nWhen the agent calls any scheduling tool (list_free_slots,\ncreate_appointment, list_patient_appointments, cancel_appointment,\nreschedule_appointment) and _issued_patient_ids is empty —\nmeaning no create_patient or lookup_patient_* has returned a\npatient_id on this call — we now:\n\n  1. broadcast `no_patient_context` so the dashboard can surface\n     the problem (already wired through the supervisor-flag\n     panel infrastructure),\n  2. inject a (system override) message via send_client_content\n     telling the agent to call create_patient (or the right\n     lookup) RIGHT NOW with the data it collected, then re-call\n     the scheduling tool, and explicitly to correct any time it\n     already quoted to the caller.\n\nA _nudged_no_patient_ctx flag prevents re-spamming the same\ncorrection on every chunk while the agent is still mid-turn.\n\nPlus a new GUARDRAIL block \"NO scheduling tool without a real\npatient_id\" so the persona reinforces the rule the runtime\nenforces. Includes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af2bed7b61bd5ddba7a224c1a5bf1786be587cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/af2bed7b61bd5ddba7a224c1a5bf1786be587cf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDIzZjliNzYyNzhkMDE4YTM4ZTEyNjIxNTM3ZGNlODUwYzBhZmVmOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce","sha":"8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce"}],"sha":"23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/23f9b76278d018a38e12621537dce850c0afef90"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T23:11:34Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"Zeyad Ibrahim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T23:11:34Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"Zeyad Ibrahim"},"message":"Supervisor escalation (AMI dial-in) + WhatsApp + persona hardening\n\nBackend:\n- ami.py: minimal asyncio AMI client; dial_supervisor with three\n  ChanSpy modes (listen/whisper/barge), Local-pair bridge-peer\n  channel discovery, no `o` option so audio works both directions.\n- wasender.py: httpx wrapper for WasenderApi — send_text,\n  list_messages, ping. Saudi phone normalisation.\n- router.py: new endpoints /agent/escalation, /agent/calls/{id}/\n  acknowledge_flag, /agent/calls/{id}/dial_supervisor?mode=,\n  /whatsapp/{status,send,chats,messages}.\n- live_agent.py: persona rewrite — context-first escalation, never\n  ask gender, today/tomorrow dates pre-injected, digit-by-digit\n  speaking rule, slot-grid discipline; CallSession.set_flag/ack_flag;\n  escalation.json loader with AMI + WasenderApi fields.\n- agent_tools.py: flag_for_supervisor tool, _format_saudi_mobile,\n  slot-grid hard reject in create/reschedule_appointment.\n- sip_live_rep.py: always-on echo gate + LOW VAD sensitivity.\n\nFrontend: deployed SPA bundle rebuilt with the new Dashboard table,\nWhatsApp inbox, and EscalationConfigCard sections.\n\nDocs:\n- DEMOSITEMAP.md: new section 6c (supervisor escalation + dial-in\n  end-to-end) and 6d (persona/tool hardening reference).\n- TOCOPY.md (new): self-contained checklist for the office machine\n  to pull, fill 6 per-machine fields from the Configuration page,\n  restart uvicorn, verify.\n- .gitignore: exclude data/demos/ (escalation.json holds secrets),\n  data/ai_camera/, .claude/settings.local.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbeea63750d2fe37bbe850de39b52be4bc0bd0ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/cbeea63750d2fe37bbe850de39b52be4bc0bd0ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDhiZGQyM2U5MTVkZTg5YWJmNDdkZWY5MzNiNWVjZjAzZDUyMWZkY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9","sha":"3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9"}],"sha":"8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8bdd23e915de89abf47def933b5ecf03d521fdce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:40:52Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:40:52Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"DEMOSITEMAP: Windows pull instructions (Git Bash + PowerShell)\n\nMachine A is Windows. Replace the bash-only pull block with two\nexplicit variants:\n\n- Git Bash (recommended) — every other snippet in this file works\n  there verbatim, with the PW_ROOT path adjusted to /c/Users/…\n- PowerShell — uses $env:PW_ROOT, Push-Location/Pop-Location, and\n  foreach instead of for.\n\nPlus a short \"Windows-only path notes\" block covering the venv\ninterpreter path (.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe vs .venv/bin/python),\nthe activation script difference, and the PowerShell equivalents\nof cp -r / rm -rf used in the build pipeline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c16bc55cd941c319c6663fa5a92ea1ded18d64d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/c16bc55cd941c319c6663fa5a92ea1ded18d64d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDMzMTVjOTZlMTliNGI2N2JmZGMxM2VkYmU4NWUwNWQ3NDY2NjBkZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936","sha":"b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936"}],"sha":"3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/3315c96e19b4b67bfdc13edbe85e05d746660dd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:39:26Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T14:39:26Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"DEMOSITEMAP: machine-A pull instructions + recent-work summary\n\nAdds a \"Switching to Machine A — what to pull, and what''s new\"\nsubsection under the Clinic-source sync state that:\n\n- Gives the exact `git pull --ff-only` loop for both repos.\n- Gives the matching status loop to verify nothing''s diverged.\n- Summarises the backend + frontend commits landed on this\n  machine since the last hand-off, in user-visible order, so\n  the Machine A session has the same context without re-reading\n  every commit message.\n- Notes that the deployed bundle under frontend/demos/clinic/\n  already matches prime-mate-clinic/src, so no rebuild is\n  required for read-only / run-only use.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"995c18cdd929370dc7f1bfd27b797baa588655f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/995c18cdd929370dc7f1bfd27b797baa588655f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGI2NGQ0ODExZDIwYjUzNjMxNzYzMjk0ODQ3Mjk1OWFkMmU4OTY5MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43","sha":"c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43"}],"sha":"b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/b64d4811d20b536317632948472959ad2e896936"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:52:50Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:52:50Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: accept ambiguous 12h/24h times in fabrication check\n\nFalse-positive from the slot-time fabrication detector. A real\nbooking at 16:30 succeeded, but the agent spoke \"4:30\" with the\nAM/PM marker dropped from Gemini''s transcription. The strict 24-\nhour parser read it as 04:30, didn''t find that in the whitelist,\nfired a correction telling the agent to apologise, so the agent\ntold the caller the booking failed even though it succeeded.\n\nFix: any HH:MM match without an AM/PM marker is treated as\ngenuinely ambiguous and gets BOTH interpretations (H and H+12 when\nH<12). The detector accepts if any interpretation is in the\nwhitelist or within the ±15 min tolerance. Only fires a\nfabrication warning when none of the candidates lands near a real\nslot — closing the false-positive that was sabotaging successful\nreschedules without weakening detection of genuinely invented\ntimes like \"6:30 PM\" when no clinic offered an 18:30 slot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"353279db2fb3ba623d9a9a33c7516046a89e9928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/353279db2fb3ba623d9a9a33c7516046a89e9928"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGM0MGU5M2JlNjNhODkxNzg2MjA1NjQxMmQ1NTk1MWNmNjQ1OTViNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e","sha":"2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e"}],"sha":"c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/c40e93be63a8917862056412d55951cf64595b43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:28:35Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:28:35Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Rebuild clinic SPA: agent mutation drain at layout level\n\nPicks up the prime-mate-clinic change that moved the agent\ntool_mutation drain from Dashboard into _app.tsx, so cancels /\nreschedules / creations apply to localStorage regardless of which\npage the user is viewing during a call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23b971f7f4503b2932f17b5599ae21bf843ec4a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/23b971f7f4503b2932f17b5599ae21bf843ec4a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDJjMWZkZGUxNGZjYTk0ZmJlNDNjNGViZWQ4NmQzNjhkY2RiODU2MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c","sha":"4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c"}],"sha":"2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/2c1fdde14fca94fbe43c4ebed86d368dcdb8561e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:22:36Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:22:36Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: reschedule/cancel tools + slot-time fabrication check\n\nUser reported two related failures during a real call:\n- Agent offered slots up to 6:30 PM when the clinic closes at 5\n- Caller picked one, agent confirmed, but no appointment changed\n  and nothing appeared in the Live Agent Activity feed\n\nRoot cause was the same: the agent had no tool to actually change\nan appointment, so it faked success; and the agent also invented\nthe slot times to offer rather than calling list_free_slots.\n\nThree structural fixes:\n\n1. Three new function tools so the change-booking flow can run\n   end to end:\n     - list_patient_appointments(patient_id, include_past?)\n       returns the caller''s actual upcoming appointments so the\n       agent picks a real appointment_id instead of inventing\n       one.\n     - cancel_appointment(appointment_id, reason?) flips status\n       to \"cancelled\", patches notes, broadcasts\n       tool_mutation kind=appointment_cancelled.\n     - reschedule_appointment(appointment_id, new_date,\n       new_time) re-runs the full create_appointment gauntlet\n       (working hours, break window, booking buffer, conflicts —\n       and now also a hard off-hours check) and broadcasts\n       tool_mutation kind=appointment_rescheduled with the\n       previous scheduled_at so the Dashboard can show\n       before/after.\n\n2. Fabrication detector now also catches appointment TIMES the\n   agent speaks. CallSession tracks _issued_slot_times — the\n   set of HH:MM values list_free_slots /\n   list_patient_appointments returned on this call. Two new\n   regexes (_TIME_AMPM, _TIME_24H) parse any clock time the\n   agent says into 24-hour HH:MM. If a spoken time isn''t in\n   the whitelist (with a ±15 min tolerance for transcription\n   noise), it''s a fabrication, and the same in-session\n   correction + Dashboard warning fires as for fabricated IDs.\n   The check only runs once at least one slot list has been\n   returned — otherwise we''d false-positive on the agent\n   mentioning the current time.\n\n3. New GUARDRAIL block \"Changing an existing booking\" tells the\n   agent exactly which tools to use for change/cancel/move\n   requests and forbids confirming any change without an\n   {ok: true} tool response. The \"Never fabricate\" block now\n   explicitly covers appointment times: never quote a slot\n   list_free_slots didn''t return.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c23b532b4926a38af16b8a153a44080fd5a0d641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/c23b532b4926a38af16b8a153a44080fd5a0d641"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDRlNGNlZjhkYWQ1NTJkNzFmMzRlOWU4YjdhNzliYzA2ZjM4NTg0M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b","sha":"8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b"}],"sha":"4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/4e4cef8dad552d71f34e9e8b7a79bc06f385843c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:03:08Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:03:08Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: name-only create_patient + must-ask intake rule\n\nTwo changes targeting the same observed failure (agent skipped\nasking for the national ID, then either fabricated a file_number\nor the create_patient call failed silently with empty args):\n\n1. create_patient is now permissive — only ''name'' is strictly\n   required. phone, id_number, dob, gender, city are all\n   accepted when present and stored empty otherwise. The\n   function declaration''s description spells out that this\n   permissiveness is a safety net (so a record still gets saved\n   when the caller refuses to share) — NOT a licence for the\n   agent to skip asking. The schema''s `required` list is\n   reduced to just [\"name\"].\n\n2. New GUARDRAIL block \"Required intake QUESTIONS — different\n   from required tool fields\" lists the six questions the agent\n   MUST ASK before calling create_patient (name → mobile →\n   national/Iqama ID → DOB → city → reason), with explicit\n   callout that asking-and-being-refused is fine but\n   never-asking is a defect. The older \"Intake — ONE field at\n   a time\" block now cross-references this list so the two\n   blocks reinforce each other instead of drifting apart.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dbaa8790b2b3356a21bee7e86d5d4be6dd576a2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/dbaa8790b2b3356a21bee7e86d5d4be6dd576a2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDhhMzM0MGYzMmI5OTZhNGYwYzhjMTkxMWE4Y2JjN2I4MzNmZWQ1NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551","sha":"9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551"}],"sha":"8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/8a3340f32b996a4f0c8c1911a8cbc7b833fed54b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:55:48Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:55:48Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: real-time fabrication detector + in-session correction\n\nPersona discipline alone was not stopping Gemini Live from\ninventing plausible-looking identifiers (e.g. agent told the\ncaller \"your file number is C345678\" without ever calling\ncreate_patient — file was never saved, nothing appeared in the\nLive Agent Activity). Add a structural guard:\n\n- CallSession tracks per-call whitelists of IDs returned by\n  successful tool calls: _issued_file_numbers,\n  _issued_appointment_ids, _issued_patient_ids. Populated from\n  create_patient / create_appointment / lookup_* responses.\n\n- A regex detector (_FILE_PATTERN [ABC]+6 digits, _APT_PATTERN\n  APT-NNN, both whitespace/hyphen tolerant) runs on every\n  output_transcription chunk, scans the accumulated spoken_text,\n  and for any match not in the whitelist:\n    1. logs a warning\n    2. broadcasts a `fabrication` WS event so the Dashboard\n       shows a prominent red panel (visible across calls)\n    3. injects a corrective system message back into the live\n       Gemini session via send_client_content — \"STOP, you\n       spoke X but no tool returned that; either call the\n       correct tool now or apologise to the caller and explain\n       reception will complete the record. Do NOT repeat the\n       fabricated value.\"\n\n- _corrected_ids set prevents spamming a correction for every\n  chunk of a single fabricated value while the agent finishes\n  speaking it.\n\nThe same channel exists for appointment_id, so the previous\n\"appointment confirmed but never created\" silent failure mode is\nclosed too.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83bf616702feb19251dfa11412636c31c2e10f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/83bf616702feb19251dfa11412636c31c2e10f10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDkwMDdkMDlhODViNGQ2OTg2ZjQyYmQwZmU2YTEwNDZlMDczYWI1NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0","sha":"7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0"}],"sha":"9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/9007d09a85b4d6986f42bd0fe6a1046e073ab551"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:42:54Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:42:54Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: stop sessions hanging after caller drops\n\nTrace from the user:\n\n    write loop ended: unable to perform operation on\n    <TCPTransport closed=True ...>; the handler is closed\n    Task exception was never retrieved (ConnectionClosedOK)\n\nTwo distinct problems were producing the symptom of calls\n\"hanging\" (session never finalising after the caller dropped):\n\n1. _write_loop and _read_loop had no `finally` setting\n   stop_evt. If Asterisk closed TCP and write() raised before\n   the read loop saw EOF, write_loop logged a warning and\n   exited — but stop_evt was never set, so CallSession.run()\n   stayed parked on `await self.stop_evt.wait()` forever. The\n   Gemini WS dangled until it timed out idle, then closed; the\n   call session never properly finalised and accumulated as a\n   zombie. Both loops now always signal stop_evt in `finally`.\n\n2. The Gemini `receive()` coroutine let\n   `ConnectionClosedOK` propagate when Gemini closed the WS\n   cleanly at end-of-call. The outer `asyncio.wait` then\n   moved the task into `done`, but nothing called `.exception()`\n   on it, so Python logged \"Task exception was never\n   retrieved\". feed() had the same shape. Both are now wrapped\n   in try/except (re-raising CancelledError) and a finally\n   that sets stop_evt. After the wait, the new loop drains\n   exceptions from completed tasks so cosmetic warnings stop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3ccb8bad4b8ac54e18197d4caedebf552346adc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/3ccb8bad4b8ac54e18197d4caedebf552346adc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDcyNzllNzVkZjdiZDFlOTA3ODA3OGMwZjMwNjFmN2E0NjM2YWQyYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7","sha":"55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7"}],"sha":"7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/7279e75df7bd1e9078078c0f3061f7a4636ad2c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:35:51Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:35:51Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: broadcast tool_result + tighten persona\n\nThree fixes for issues from a real test call:\n\n1. Agent told the caller \"your appointment is confirmed\" but the\n   create_appointment tool had actually returned an error — the\n   booking never happened and nothing appeared in the Live Agent\n   Activity feed because broadcast was only firing on SUCCESS.\n   Now every tool call broadcasts a `tool_result` event with\n   {ok, error, args}, so the Dashboard can show failures in real\n   time. Combined with a new always-on GUARDRAIL line (\"NEVER\n   say ''your appointment is confirmed'' UNLESS create_appointment\n   just returned a response containing an appointment_id\") the\n   silent-failure failure mode is closed at both ends.\n\n2. Agent spoke times as \"16:00\" — military format the caller\n   shouldn''t be reading off a phone call. New GUARDRAIL block\n   \"Time format — speak 12-hour, with AM/PM\" with English and\n   Arabic forms (\"4:00 PM\" / \"الرابعة عصراً\"). Tools still use\n   24-hour internally; the agent translates when speaking.\n\n3. Agent asked for name, mobile, ID, DOB, and city in one\n   breath. New GUARDRAIL block \"Intake — ONE field at a time,\n   confirm each before moving on\" with a recommended order and\n   the explicit rule to read each field back before moving on.\n\nAll three rules land in _GUARDRAILS so a customised on-disk\npersona can''t bypass them.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"21b20ef89ddc2e81892ef89d1cf85d04698802ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/21b20ef89ddc2e81892ef89d1cf85d04698802ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDU1NjU0ZThiODE2NWM0YzJmNWIyNmQ5NGFjMGM3MGExOTRkMGQwYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc","sha":"37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc"}],"sha":"55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/55654e8b8165c4c2f5b26d94ac0c70a194d0d0a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:24:31Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:24:31Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: stop faking file numbers + transliterate names\n\nThree bugs from a real test call:\n\n1. Agent invented a file number (''A123456'') and claimed it had\n   created the patient — but the create_patient tool had actually\n   errored out (the caller hadn''t given a valid id_number, and\n   the tool required one). Fix in two layers:\n   - Loosen create_patient: only ''name'' and ''phone'' are strictly\n     required now. id_number, dob, gender, city are accepted when\n     provided but no longer block the create — a record with\n     \"fill in at reception\" gaps is better than no record at all,\n     and FAR better than the agent inventing a file number to\n     save face.\n   - Add a \"Never fabricate a tool result\" block to the always-on\n     GUARDRAILS: file_number / appointment_id / patient_id MUST\n     come from the literal JSON body of a successful tool\n     response on this call. Quoting plausible-looking values is\n     forbidden. On tool error, the agent must apologise honestly\n     and either retry or defer to reception.\n\n2. Agent asked the caller to spell their name in English. New\n   \"Filling forms — agent-side, not caller-side\" block tells the\n   agent to romanise the caller''s Arabic name itself (Fahad,\n   Mohammed, …), infer gender from voice / honorifics, and pass\n   empty strings for optional fields the caller couldn''t supply.\n\nBoth blocks land in _GUARDRAILS (appended after persona on every\ncall) so a customised persona can''t bypass them, and the\ncreate_patient function declaration''s `description` now spells\nout that name is the agent''s transliteration job, not the\ncaller''s.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"985c6cb95fdf120aee8646960c47309241e3b98e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/985c6cb95fdf120aee8646960c47309241e3b98e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDM3NzY0ZDA5YmQ3ZjM4NzUwYTY2MTIyMDYyODQzNDhkN2NkMmI0Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341","sha":"7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341"}],"sha":"37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/37764d09bd7f38750a6612206284348d7cd2b4cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:16:45Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:16:45Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: structural anti-hallucination + privacy guardrails\n\nThe agent was making up clinics that don''t exist and inventing\ndoctor names. Three layers of defense:\n\n1. Two new function tools — list_clinics(specialty?) and\n   list_providers(specialty?, clinic_id?, role?) — so the agent\n   has a way to *check* before claiming. Both filter the\n   snapshot.json roster and return only active rows, with a\n   trailing \"These are the ONLY X — do not invent others\" note.\n\n2. Per-call system instruction now injects the actual clinic +\n   provider rosters from snapshot.json as AVAILABLE CLINICS and\n   ON-STAFF PROVIDERS blocks. This is the structural defense —\n   the model can''t drift away from data that''s literally in its\n   prompt.\n\n3. Always-on _GUARDRAILS block appended after the persona text\n   (BEFORE the KB) so even a customised persona saved via \"Apply\n   to Live Agent\" can''t bypass the anti-fabrication and patient-\n   privacy rules. Specifically:\n   - lookup_patient_* output is for identity verification only;\n     the agent may NOT read another patient''s data out loud.\n   - \"I don''t have that information\" is always a valid answer.\n\nDEFAULT_PERSONA in both repos is updated to match, but the\nbackend guardrail block is the load-bearing piece — persona text\ncan be edited freely without weakening privacy or grounding.\n\nIncludes the rebuilt clinic SPA bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc8a1458cbf44fbe7ebdbde835ca2b0a3e606bea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/bc8a1458cbf44fbe7ebdbde835ca2b0a3e606bea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDdlYWQ5OTczMzBkN2VlYmVkM2YyNWEwNzljYTg2YjJmMDZkMDMzNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5","sha":"6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5"}],"sha":"7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/7ead997330d7eebed3f25a079ca86b2f06d03341"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:08:05Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T11:08:05Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic agent: mixed.wav + Gemini offline transcript enhancement\n\nTwo pieces of post-call work the History page asked for:\n\n1. mixed.wav — overlay the agent timeline onto the caller timeline\n   using audioop.add sample-by-sample, written next to the existing\n   caller.wav / agent.wav. agent.wav is also now rendered in real\n   call time (silence between speech) instead of back-to-back chunks\n   so it lines up with caller.wav. Each agent chunk is timestamped\n   in CallSession._write_loop with (offset_s, bytes) so the mixer\n   knows where to place it.\n\n2. Offline transcript enhancement — after _save_recording the\n   service spawns _enhance_transcript as a background task. It\n   reads mixed.wav and calls client.aio.models.generate_content\n   (gemini-2.5-flash → 2.0-flash → 1.5-flash fallback) with a\n   response_schema of [{role, text}], merges the result into\n   meta.json as `enhanced_turns` with `enhanced_status`. Live\n   capture is preserved so the History page can fall back to it\n   when the enhancement is pending/failed.\n\n`/agent/calls/{id}/audio/{side}` now accepts `mixed` as a side, and\nlist_saved_calls exposes `has_mixed_wav` + `enhanced_status` so the\nSPA knows when to show the Full call player and when to keep\npolling for the cleaner transcript.\n\nAlso rebuilds the clinic SPA bundle in frontend/demos/clinic/\n(History page wires the new mixed audio + enhanced transcript\nbanner; same commit on the prime-mate-clinic source repo).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e906a6bc7f06e255036aee97316e96be00aa578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/0e906a6bc7f06e255036aee97316e96be00aa578"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDZmOTUzMTI0MThmOTNkNGNhOGYxYTVjOTg4MDg3M2U2MDg5NWIxYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045","sha":"516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045"}],"sha":"6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/6f95312418f93d4ca8f1a5c9880873e60895b1b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:47:38Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:47:38Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"clinic agent: APT id width=3 (match SPA) + persona discipline\n\nagent_tools._next_id no longer takes a width arg; it derives width\nfrom the prefix (PAT=4 to match patient id width, everything else=3).\nAPT IDs now match the SPA''s APT-NNN format — previous APT-NNNN\nwould have collided with nothing but rendered weirdly in mixed\nlists. Also normalized scheduled_at to include the trailing :00\nseconds so slice(11,16) always lands on HH:MM.\n\nBackend default persona mirrors the SPA''s seed updates:\n- end_call: NEVER right after create_appointment/create_patient\n- VERBATIM tool readbacks, letter by letter for file_number\n- \"Never say\" list: no administration transfer, no fabrication\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6ebb729583b7febc531ba0e0c7eb9e59100f97f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/a6ebb729583b7febc531ba0e0c7eb9e59100f97f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDUxNmU0YWQ4YzA3NWZiMTE2NzliZjFiZDA0OTRjZDNjOWE2NmUwNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb","sha":"753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb"}],"sha":"516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/516e4ad8c075fb11679bf1bd0494cd3c9a66e045"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:33:02Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:33:02Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"clinic agent: fix _DATA_DIR path (parents[4], not [3])\n\nlive_agent.py and agent_tools.py live three levels under backend/app\n(backend/app/demos/clinic/), so parents[3] resolved to backend/\ninstead of the project root. That''s why my previous commit\naccidentally created backend/data/demos/clinic/calls/... and dragged\ntest WAVs into git. Bumped to parents[4] so the data dir is the\ncanonical PWDemoMaster/data/demos/clinic/ that lives alongside\nstate.json and the rest. Removed the stray test recordings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8423cd223108108b1e086e30b80bb3a5b749b8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/8423cd223108108b1e086e30b80bb3a5b749b8fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDc1M2E2OTYyYmMyMGQxODdlODFmOTg4OTdkMTk3MjYxODNiZmJjZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51","sha":"97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51"}],"sha":"753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/753a6962bc20d187e81f98897d19726183bfbceb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:31:43Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:31:43Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic Live Agent: function-call tools + snapshot sync + time awareness\n\nNEW MODULE backend/app/demos/clinic/agent_tools.py — exposes 7\nGemini Live function tools and persists clinic data to a snapshot.\n\nTOOLS (declared via build_tools(), dispatched via\nexecute_tool(name, args, ctx)):\n- lookup_patient_by_phone(phone) — loose match, strips formatting,\n  matches Saudi numbers with or without country code\n- lookup_patient_by_id_number(id_number) — 10-digit national/Iqama\n- lookup_patient_by_file_number(file_number) — A/B/C + 6 digits\n- list_free_slots(date, clinic_id=null) — already filters past\n  times AND any slot within 15 minutes of now (\"today\" only)\n- create_patient(...) — appends to snapshot, broadcasts\n  tool_mutation\n- create_appointment(patient_id, clinic_id, date, time, …) —\n  re-verifies slot is free + non-break + within hours + outside\n  the buffer before writing; broadcasts tool_mutation\n- end_call(reason) — sets tool_ctx[\"end_requested\"]; the receive\n  loop schedules a 3 s delayed stop so the agent''s spoken goodbye\n  actually leaves the wire\n\nSNAPSHOT (data/demos/clinic/snapshot.json) — the Clinic SPA''s\nDashboard POSTs full state to /api/demo/clinic/data/snapshot on\nmount + on any change. New router endpoints:\n- GET  /api/demo/clinic/data/snapshot\n- POST /api/demo/clinic/data/snapshot\n\nLIVE_AGENT integration:\n- _build_system_instruction now appends a ## CURRENT TIME block\n  with the local date, weekday (en + ar), and current HH:MM TZ.\n  Persona instructs the agent to trust this and never invent a day.\n- LiveConnectConfig now includes tools=build_tools().\n- receive() loop handles resp.tool_call: dispatch each\n  FunctionCall, broadcast tool_call + caller_identified events,\n  collect FunctionResponses, send_tool_response.\n- CallSession._delayed_stop(s) helper for graceful end_call.\n\nPERSONA — both the seed (clinicLiveData.ts) and the backend\ndefault (live_agent.py DEFAULT_PERSONA) updated:\n- Arabic gender default is MASCULINE; switch to feminine only\n  after hearing a female voice.\n- Time references say \"today\" / \"اليوم\", never the day name.\n- \"Never offer a slot in the past or within 15 minutes of now\"\n  with the system buffer matching the tool''s enforcement.\n- End-of-call: agent MUST call end_call() after the goodbye line.\n- \"Tools — use them, don''t fake them\" section.\n\nDEMOSITEMAP §6b updated with the full three-flow sync model\n(snapshot push, tool_mutation broadcast, caller_identified\nresolution), the tools table, the time-awareness contract, the\nend_call delayed-stop mechanics, and the singleton WS store\nthat keeps the Dashboard transcript alive across navigation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b7be3b6db043e750d11e0f1cf6b7aa37993c724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/7b7be3b6db043e750d11e0f1cf6b7aa37993c724"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKDk3ZTYyYTdmZjk0MGZiNGYzMTQ3MGE1MGY1MzE5NWM5MzUzMDJjNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765","sha":"d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765"}],"sha":"97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/97e62a7ff940fb4f31470a50f53195c935302c51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:14:49Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T10:14:49Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"Clinic Live Agent: WAV + transcript recording + History API + persona\n\n- backend/app/demos/clinic/live_agent.py\n  - CallSession captures the raw 8 kHz caller frames (pre-resample)\n    and the 8 kHz agent frames (post-resample, immediately before\n    AudioSocket send) so recordings round-trip lossless.\n  - Appends each transcript fragment into a role-collapsed turns[]\n    list so consecutive same-speaker chunks become one entry.\n  - On hangup: ClinicLiveAgentService._handle now calls\n    _save_recording(session), which writes caller.wav + agent.wav\n    + meta.json to data/demos/clinic/calls/<id>/. Empty calls (no\n    audio + no transcript — usually probes) are skipped.\n  - New module helpers: list_saved_calls, load_saved_call,\n    call_audio_path, delete_saved_call.\n  - DEFAULT_PERSONA matches the SPA-side seed: includes the\n    intake-flow script (phone lookup → new/existing → file # or\n    cross-confirm name+DOB+ID → only-then book).\n\n- backend/app/demos/clinic/router.py — new endpoints:\n    GET    /api/demo/clinic/agent/calls               — list\n    GET    /api/demo/clinic/agent/calls/{id}          — full meta\n    GET    /api/demo/clinic/agent/calls/{id}/audio/{caller|agent}\n    DELETE /api/demo/clinic/agent/calls/{id}\n  Adds the `call_ended` WS event a `saved_call_id` field so the\n  Dashboard / History page can correlate live → recorded.\n\n- DEMOSITEMAP §6b: documents the recording layout (caller.wav /\n  agent.wav / meta.json), the new endpoints, the Patient id_number\n  field, and a refreshed Open Follow-ups list calling out the\n  remaining work (function-call tools, CALLERID→AudioSocket UUID\n  bridge, real-event activity feed sync).\n\n- frontend/demos/clinic: rebuild from prime-mate-clinic@HEAD —\n  Dashboard wired to /agent/ws (real active calls + transcript),\n  new History page + sidebar entry, Patient ID # column +\n  validated input + suggestIdNumber.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50da20bff591855d669d87b49a24fa9b9b184f7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/50da20bff591855d669d87b49a24fa9b9b184f7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765","node_id":"C_kwDOSbdVDNoAKGQ4MzFkYjdiMzRjYzEyZGFiOGFkZDBhMGQxY2UxNDM2YzAzMmQ3NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commit/d37ad936a58156cc7bd9ada6c9494166207ceea4","sha":"d37ad936a58156cc7bd9ada6c9494166207ceea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d37ad936a58156cc7bd9ada6c9494166207ceea4"}],"sha":"d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d831db7b34cc12dab8add0a0d1ce1436c032d765"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/commits/d37ad936a58156cc7bd9ada6c9494166207ceea4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T09:57:23Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T09:57:23Z","email":"z_buh@hotmail.com","name":"ZeyadA"},"message":"DEMOSITEMAP: fix clinic dialplan — valid UUID + Wait(0.3)\n\nThe clinic dialplan I documented in §6b used a 48-char string for\nAUDIOSOCKET_UUID (clinic-demo-00000000-…). app_audiosocket validates\nthe UUID format strictly and hangs up the call if it isn''t an exact\n8-4-4-4-12 hex UUID. User hit this — dial 9001 dropped immediately.\n\nUpdated the example to use 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333\n(matching the admin SLA''s 1111-… and SLR''s 2222-… so the clinic\nservice logs are easy to spot at a glance) and added the Wait(0.3)\nbetween Answer() and AudioSocket() that the working dialplans use\nto avoid early-RTP frame drops.\n\nAlso added a two-bullet \"things this dialplan gets right\" callout\nso the next vertical (Restaurant on port 8093) doesn''t repeat the\nmistake.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c247a13aae12128c910a9eec85f6b7952cbd342f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/trees/c247a13aae12128c910a9eec85f6b7952cbd342f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheJan2020/pw-demo-master/git/commits/d37ad936a58156cc7bd9ada6c9494166207ceea4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64112255?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheJan2020","id":64112255,"login":"TheJan2020","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTEyMjU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheJan2020/received_events","repos_ur