om/repos/mosandlt/ioBroker.bosch-smart-home-camera/commits/4cc8a3f1a61794d410154582a1682a3206862475/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T03:35:21Z","email":"10558666+mosandlt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mosandlt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T03:35:21Z","email":"10558666+mosandlt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"mosandlt"},"message":"v1.3.0: VIS-2 React camera widget (live video) + livestream-stability fix\n\nNew VIS-2 \"Bosch Camera\" widget (React / Module Federation, built from\nsrc-widgets/ with Vite + @module-federation/vite). Three stream modes:\nsnapshot (near-live), live MJPEG (play button → frames from the local RTSP\nproxy via a new web_stream backend over uiClientSubscribe/sendToUI), and\ngo2rtc WebRTC. iOS/Android frosted control bar (privacy, livestream, light,\nsnapshot, pan, privacy-sound, siren) with privacy gating, portal-based\nfullscreen, real camera names and a clear offline state. Pan only on the\nGen1 360° indoor (hardware_version INDOOR).\n\nFix: RTSP proxy no longer tears down ~60 s after start when the livestream is\nenabled during a snapshot (snapshot idle-teardown armed with a stale flag);\nre-read the live flag in finally. Regression test added.\n\nRegistration: io-package visWidgets name = MF remote name, bundlerType=module,\ni18n=component; getWidgetInfo().visSet + view widgetSet = adapter name (required\nfor vis-2 to load the set).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f23205186f4497fee7afe59df80e63baf6496ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mosandlt/ioBroker.bosch-smart-home-camera/git/trees/4f23205186f4497fee7afe59df80e63baf6496ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mosandlt/ioBroker.bosch-smart-home-camera/git/commits/4cc8a3f1a61794d410154582a1682a3206862475","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10558666?v=4","events_